01:15:45.440 --> 01:15:48.773
Well, there's your press agent.
Talk to him about it.

1217
01:15:51.312 --> 01:15:53.246
I come in peace.
I don't want any trouble.

1218
01:15:53.348 --> 01:15:55.316
I really don't want to talk to you
right now, Paul. Not now.

1219
01:15:55.417 --> 01:15:59.353
- Just trying to do my job.
- Oh, really? Well, now I can't do mine.

1220
01:15:59.454 --> 01:16:01.479
We're already screwed with
the amount of tips we got on this thing,

1221
01:16:01.589 --> 01:16:03.284
and you just freaked out the entire state.

1222
01:16:03.391 --> 01:16:06.690
I have got Napa, Vallejo, and DOJ
looking at me sideways

1223
01:16:06.795 --> 01:16:09.593
and Riverside's telling me
I'm on a snipe hunt!

1224
01:16:09.698 --> 01:16:12.326
Jesus. Hey, Cheri Jo Bates was a gift.
I gave that to you.

1225
01:16:12.434 --> 01:16:13.992
You and Armstrong
never would have found her.

1226
01:16:14.102 --> 01:16:16.366
This may not be Zodiac.
Does that matter to you?

1227
01:16:16.471 --> 01:16:17.802
- What if it is?
- Does it matter that Riverside may not

1228
01:16:17.906 --> 01:16:19.965
be able to make a case
against their suspect because of you?

1229
01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:21.975
Tell it to Sherwood.
I'm out here, beating the bushes,

1230
01:16:22.077 --> 01:16:23.635
trying to draw him out.
We're in this together.

1231
01:16:23.745 --> 01:16:25.110
No, we're not in anything together, Paul,

1232
01:16:25.213 --> 01:16:27.078
because I'm not interested
in upping my circulation.

1233
01:16:27.182 --> 01:16:30.049
Oh, boy. He wrote me.
He threatened my life.

1234
01:16:30.151 --> 01:16:31.743
Hey, Bullitt!

1235
01:16:31.853 --> 01:16:35.812
Been a year-and-a-half,
you gonna catch this fucking guy or not?

1236
01:16:37.959 --> 01:16:40.325
- Go fuck yourself.
- Happily.

1237
01:16:40.428 --> 01:16:42.419
You should have called me, Paul.

1238
01:16:48.002 --> 01:16:49.196
Thank you.

1239
01:17:02.484 --> 01:17:04.213
- Did you see this?
- Unfortunately, yes.

1240
01:17:04.319 --> 01:17:06.981
Here comes every lunatic in California.

1241
01:17:07.856 --> 01:17:09.153
I'm the Zodiac.

1242
01:17:09.257 --> 01:17:10.815
And how did you kill your victims?

1243
01:17:10.925 --> 01:17:13.553
With a gun. No, with a hammer.

1244
01:17:13.661 --> 01:17:14.958
All I'm authorized to tell you

1245
01:17:15.063 --> 01:17:16.621
is that he's still under
government employment.

1246
01:17:16.731 --> 01:17:19.791
- And who authorized you to tell me this?
- That's all I'm authorized to say.

1247
01:17:19.901 --> 01:17:22.028
Only a little rat bastard like Andre

1248
01:17:22.137 --> 01:17:24.697
could have done something
like cut off all the victims' hands.

1249
01:17:24.806 --> 01:17:27.172
Zodiac didn't cut off
any of the victims' hands.

1250
01:17:27.275 --> 01:17:29.004
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.

1251
01:17:29.110 --> 01:17:31.635
Travis and I worked here
side by side for 10 years.

1252
01:17:31.746 --> 01:17:35.807
His foot gets crushed in an accident
and the killings begin.

1253
01:17:35.917 --> 01:17:37.407
- Coincidence?
- I don't know.

1254
01:17:37.519 --> 01:17:39.384
You're a cop, man. Do the math.

1255
01:17:43.792 --> 01:17:47.023
Have you considered
the killer might be Paul Avery?

1256
01:17:47.128 --> 01:17:48.288
Frequently.

1257
01:17:48.897 --> 01:17:50.262
He was drinking Coors,
getting a load on.

1258
01:17:50.832 --> 01:17:54.461
Starts talking about hunting people.
Like that book.

1259
01:17:54.569 --> 01:17:56.730
Says how you can put a light
at the end of a gun

1260
01:17:56.838 --> 01:17:58.362
to use as a sight in the dark.

1261
01:17:58.473 --> 01:18:00.236
- He said that?
- Yeah.

1262
01:18:00.341 --> 01:18:03.208
So I asked him,
"How would you get away with it?"

1263
01:18:03.478 --> 01:18:05.207
And he said, "It would be easy

1264
01:18:05.313 --> 01:18:07.747
"'cause there'd be no real motive
to the thing."

1265
01:18:07.849 --> 01:18:09.714
Then he said he'd write letters
to the police

1266
01:18:09.818 --> 01:18:11.615
and call himself Zodiac
to mess with them.

1267
01:18:11.719 --> 01:18:13.311
Leigh liked messing with people.

1268
01:18:13.421 --> 01:18:16.413
- You're positive he said "Zodiac"?
- Yeah.

1269
01:18:16.524 --> 01:18:19.618
I thought it was a stupid name.
So I told him.

1270
01:18:19.727 --> 01:18:23.163
He got up all upset and said,
"I don't care what you think.

1271
01:18:23.264 --> 01:18:25.892
"I've thought about it a long time
and that's the name I'm gonna use."

1272
01:18:26.000 --> 01:18:29.333
Did you feel like he'd been
thinking about it a long time?

1273
01:18:29.437 --> 01:18:32.668
He was raw about losing his job
at the school.

1274
01:18:32.774 --> 01:18:35.766
He talked about shooting out
the tires of a school bus

1275
01:18:35.877 --> 01:18:38.277
and picking off the little darlings.

1276
01:18:38.379 --> 01:18:42.440
- He actually used those words?
- That's what made me remember.

1277
01:18:42.550 --> 01:18:44.984
Afterwards, I told my wife
I didn't wanna see him again.

1278
01:18:45.086 --> 01:18:46.815
And I haven't since.

1279
01:18:46.921 --> 01:18:49.412
Other thing is, Leigh's into skin diving.

1280
01:18:49.524 --> 01:18:51.583
I know he's been up to that lake
a bunch of times.

1281
01:18:51.693 --> 01:18:54.059
Lake Berryessa?
Did you ever go with him?

1282
01:18:54.162 --> 01:18:58.121
Couple times. We went fishing
by Putah Creek near there.

1283
01:18:58.233 --> 01:18:59.700
Tell him when you put it together.

1284
01:18:59.801 --> 01:19:04.500
About a year ago, in the paper,
there was a story about the Zodiac.

1285
01:19:04.606 --> 01:19:07.700
And it all comes back.
I tried to call the local cops.

1286
01:19:07.809 --> 01:19:09.401
They blew him off.
Thought he was a nut.

1287
01:19:09.510 --> 01:19:13.310
And you're sure
the conversation you had about Zodiac

1288
01:19:13.414 --> 01:19:17.180
took place on January 1st, 1968?

1289
01:19:17.285 --> 01:19:19.014
It couldn't have been any later.

1290
01:19:19.120 --> 01:19:22.021
I started a new job in L.A.
On January 20th.

1291
01:19:22.557 --> 01:19:24.024
I had to move.

1292
01:19:24.125 --> 01:19:26.593
- This is my problem. This guy...
- Arthur Leigh Allen?

1293
01:19:26.694 --> 01:19:29.288
This guy, Leigh,
just lays out his entire evil plan

1294
01:19:29.397 --> 01:19:30.887
to a fishing buddy on New Year's Day?

1295
01:19:30.999 --> 01:19:33.797
I don't know.
He's angry, he's been drinking,

1296
01:19:33.902 --> 01:19:36.029
been thinking about it for a while.
I can buy that.

1297
01:19:36.137 --> 01:19:38.469
So why didn't Cheney
contact us sooner?

1298
01:19:38.573 --> 01:19:40.006
I checked. He did.

1299
01:19:40.108 --> 01:19:43.100
First recorded contact
with the police department about Allen

1300
01:19:43.211 --> 01:19:46.009
was in Pomona. January 10th, 1970.

1301
01:19:46.114 --> 01:19:47.206
He just got lost in the shuffle.

1302
01:19:47.315 --> 01:19:48.976
Did Cheney have anything
against Allen?

1303
01:19:49.083 --> 01:19:50.380
Did Allen screw his wife or anything?

1304
01:19:50.485 --> 01:19:52.180
We're gonna do
a full background check.

1305
01:19:52.287 --> 01:19:54.949
But I got to tell you, I like this guy.

1306
01:19:55.990 --> 01:19:57.890
So, let's pull
some handwriting samples.

1307
01:19:59.627 --> 01:20:02.528
Hi. I talked to Sherwood.
He got the samples.

1308
01:20:02.630 --> 01:20:04.564
- What are you having?
- BLT.

1309
01:20:07.201 --> 01:20:09.726
So, the check stubs are a wash.
There's not enough handwriting.

1310
01:20:09.837 --> 01:20:12.362
The application's got more,
but it doesn't look like Z's,

1311
01:20:12.473 --> 01:20:14.771
so he can't rule him in.
But he can't rule him out, either.

1312
01:20:14.876 --> 01:20:17.743
- Well, that's vague.
- He needs more samples.

1313
01:20:18.813 --> 01:20:20.906
Also, our guy is a pervert.

1314
01:20:21.983 --> 01:20:23.848
When Mel got the application
from Valley Springs,

1315
01:20:23.952 --> 01:20:26.216
they told him that
Allen had been fired for touching kids.

1316
01:20:26.321 --> 01:20:28.448
- Touching?
- Polite euphemism.

1317
01:20:30.124 --> 01:20:33.252
- So what do you want to do?
- Make some phone calls.

1318
01:20:33.361 --> 01:20:35.989
- Are you done with the fries?
- Go ahead.

1319
01:20:36.097 --> 01:20:37.530
Did you and Mr. Cheney have a chance

1320
01:20:37.632 --> 01:20:39.827
to look at the copies
of the Zodiac letters we sent you?

1321
01:20:39.934 --> 01:20:42.630
Yeah.
Some of this stuff is pretty creepy.

1322
01:20:42.737 --> 01:20:45.831
- Yeah, we know that.
- I mean, creepy like Leigh.

1323
01:20:46.207 --> 01:20:48.698
He misspells words like that.
He thinks it's funny.

1324
01:20:48.810 --> 01:20:50.607
What about the handwriting?

1325
01:20:50.712 --> 01:20:53.647
I don't know.
Don't you have experts for that stuff?

1326
01:20:53.748 --> 01:20:56.842
Our man at Questioned Documents
says it's inconclusive.

1327
01:20:56.951 --> 01:20:58.782
Maybe he did it with his other hand.

1328
01:20:58.886 --> 01:21:00.148
The letters are a little too neat

1329
01:21:00.254 --> 01:21:02.654
for someone to have written
with the wrong hand.

1330
01:21:02.757 --> 01:21:04.486
But not for Leigh, right.

1331
01:21:04.592 --> 01:21:06.492
- What do you mean?
- He's ambidextrous.

1332
01:21:06.594 --> 01:21:09.995
He can write with either hand.
Didn't you guys know that?

1333
01:21:10.098 --> 01:21:12.896
In everyday life, Allen uses his left hand.

1334
01:21:13.001 --> 01:21:15.435
Job applications,
letters to friends, et cetera.

1335
01:21:15.536 --> 01:21:18.164
But he writes the Zodiac letters
with his right hand

1336
01:21:18.272 --> 01:21:22.038
producing a different handwriting
that he can't be linked to.

1337
01:21:22.510 --> 01:21:23.841
We got to see this guy, Chief.

1338
01:21:23.945 --> 01:21:25.139
- Where is he?
- Vallejo.

1339
01:21:25.246 --> 01:21:28.306
He works at Union Oil in Pinole.
His brother's up there, too.

1340
01:21:28.416 --> 01:21:29.849
See them both.

1341
01:21:29.951 --> 01:21:32.419
Make sure you call Mulanax.
It is his backyard.

1342
01:21:32.520 --> 01:21:35.683
Oh, right, because that
worked so well for us in Riverside.

1343
01:21:35.790 --> 01:21:38.350
Cooperation, that's us, at all costs.

1344
01:21:47.969 --> 01:21:51.996
You can talk to him in here.
Coke machine's busted, by the way.

1345
01:21:53.174 --> 01:21:55.108
I'll go get him for you.

1346
01:21:56.611 --> 01:21:58.738
So how do you guys wanna do this?

1347
01:21:58.846 --> 01:22:02.475
Well, Bill talked to the informants.
He leads, we follow?

1348
01:22:02.583 --> 01:22:04.175
It's okay by me.

1349
01:22:18.099 --> 01:22:20.659
Mr. Allen, I'm Inspector Bill Armstrong.

1350
01:22:20.768 --> 01:22:23.669
This is Inspector Dave Toschi
and Sergeant Jack Mulanax.

1351
01:22:23.771 --> 01:22:28.140
We're investigating the Zodiac murders
in San Francisco and Vallejo.

1352
01:22:28.242 --> 01:22:29.834
Please, sit down.

1353
01:22:38.719 --> 01:22:41.187
The informant notified us
that you made certain statements

1354
01:22:41.289 --> 01:22:43.849
11 months prior
to the first Zodiac murder.

1355
01:22:43.958 --> 01:22:46.984
If they're true,
they're quite incriminating.

1356
01:22:47.095 --> 01:22:49.325
Do you recall
having any such conversation?

1357
01:22:49.430 --> 01:22:50.522
- No.
- Have you ever read

1358
01:22:50.631 --> 01:22:52.599
or heard anything about the Zodiac?

1359
01:22:52.700 --> 01:22:53.928
When it was first in the paper.

1360
01:22:54.035 --> 01:22:56.094
But I didn't follow it
after those first reports.

1361
01:22:56.204 --> 01:22:58.695
- Why not?
- Too morbid. I...

1362
01:22:59.707 --> 01:23:02.505
I told all this to the other officer.

1363
01:23:02.610 --> 01:23:05.078
- Which other officer?
- From Vallejo.

1364
01:23:06.514 --> 01:23:07.947
Do you remember his name?

1365
01:23:08.049 --> 01:23:11.746
No, but it was right after
the murder at the lake.

1366
01:23:11.853 --> 01:23:14.321
And what did you tell this officer?

1367
01:23:15.923 --> 01:23:20.121
I told him that I'd gone to Salt Point
that weekend to skin dive.

1368
01:23:20.228 --> 01:23:23.026
That I was alone
but I met a couple there.

1369
01:23:24.232 --> 01:23:26.359
I have their names at home
if you want them.

1370
01:23:26.467 --> 01:23:28.094
That would be great, Arthur.

1371
01:23:28.202 --> 01:23:30.067
- Leigh.
- What?

1372
01:23:30.972 --> 01:23:33.463
Leigh. Nobody calls me Arthur.

1373
01:23:35.243 --> 01:23:38.644
Also, that day when I came home,
my neighbor saw me.

1374
01:23:38.746 --> 01:23:42.512
It was around 4:00.
But I forgot to tell the other officer that.

1375
01:23:42.617 --> 01:23:44.778
- Neighbor's name?
- Bill White.

1376
01:23:46.621 --> 01:23:48.384
He died a week or so afterwards.

1377
01:23:48.489 --> 01:23:51.890
Heart attack.
So I didn't think to call to follow up.

1378
01:23:54.061 --> 01:23:56.154
The knives I had in my car
with the blood on them,

1379
01:23:56.264 --> 01:23:59.791
that blood came from a chicken
that I killed for dinner.

1380
01:24:02.603 --> 01:24:05.401
- What?
- I had knives in my car that weekend.

1381
01:24:05.506 --> 01:24:09.772
Maybe Bill saw them
and called the other officer on me.

1382
01:24:10.411 --> 01:24:13.471
Well, we'll be checking in on that.

1383
01:24:13.581 --> 01:24:15.014
Well, let me ask you something else.

1384
01:24:15.116 --> 01:24:19.052
Were you ever in Southern California
at any time in 1966?

1385
01:24:20.087 --> 01:24:22.578
- Is this about the Riverside killing?
- Yes.

1386
01:24:23.724 --> 01:24:25.954
Well, I guess I was there
around that time.

1387
01:24:26.060 --> 01:24:29.393
I used to go down there a lot.
I like the auto races.

1388
01:24:33.734 --> 01:24:36.168
Informant says that
you're ambidextrous?

1389
01:24:36.270 --> 01:24:38.204
No, that's untrue.

1390
01:24:38.306 --> 01:24:40.604
You can't write with both hands?

1391
01:24:41.776 --> 01:24:44.836
My teachers tried to make me
when I was a kid, but I couldn't.

1392
01:24:44.946 --> 01:24:47.039
I'm left-handed.

1393
01:24:47.148 --> 01:24:51.312
He also said that you made statements
about killing school children.

1394
01:24:52.019 --> 01:24:53.509
That is...

1395
01:24:53.621 --> 01:24:56.886
That is horrible. That is...
That's a horrible thing to say.

1396
01:24:56.991 --> 01:25:00.188
So, you weren't angry
about being fired from Valley Springs

1397
01:25:00.294 --> 01:25:02.489
for touching your students?

1398
01:25:11.772 --> 01:25:13.467
I'm not the Zodiac.

1399
01:25:14.442 --> 01:25:17.411
And if I was, I certainly wouldn't tell you.

1400
01:25:19.680 --> 01:25:21.477
That's a nice watch.

1401
01:25:23.317 --> 01:25:24.341
Thank you.

1402
01:25:24.452 --> 01:25:25.885
May I see it?

1403
01:25:27.822 --> 01:25:29.255
May I see it?

1404
01:25:41.102 --> 01:25:42.160
Where'd you get it?

1405
01:25:42.370 --> 01:25:45.100
It was a Christmas gift
from my mother two years ago.

1406
01:25:45.206 --> 01:25:47.333
That's very sweet.

1407
01:25:47.441 --> 01:25:50.035
So, tell me something, Arthur.

1408
01:25:50.144 --> 01:25:51.168
You don't remember anyone

1409
01:25:51.279 --> 01:25:55.113
you might have had a conversation with
regarding the Zodiac?

1410
01:25:56.284 --> 01:26:01.688
Maybe Ted Kidder or Phil Tucker
at Vallejo Recreation.

1411
01:26:02.990 --> 01:26:04.821
But I couldn't be positive.

1412
01:26:04.925 --> 01:26:07.052
I used to work there when...

1413
01:26:10.731 --> 01:26:12.790
The Most Dangerous Game.

1414
01:26:14.101 --> 01:26:15.193
What?

1415
01:26:15.303 --> 01:26:18.466
The Most Dangerous Game.
That's why you're here, isn't it?

1416
01:26:18.572 --> 01:26:20.301
It was my favorite book in high school.

1417
01:26:20.408 --> 01:26:23.866
It's about this man who waits for people
to get shipwrecked on this island.

1418
01:26:23.978 --> 01:26:25.377
Because he was
tired of hunting animals,

1419
01:26:25.479 --> 01:26:27.071
he hunted the people for the challenge.

1420
01:26:27.181 --> 01:26:31.311
And man is the most
dangerous animal of all?

1421
01:26:31.419 --> 01:26:33.910
That's the whole point of the story.

1422
01:26:34.622 --> 01:26:35.953
Great book.

1423
01:26:37.191 --> 01:26:39.819
Or, at least, that's what I told Phil.

1424
01:26:45.433 --> 01:26:46.661
May I go?

1425
01:26:50.304 --> 01:26:51.362
Sure.

1426
01:26:56.243 --> 01:27:00.509
- Thanks for your time.
- I'm willing to help in any way possible.

1427
01:27:00.614 --> 01:27:02.673
I look forward to the day

1428
01:27:02.783 --> 01:27:06.241
when police officers
are no longer referred to as pigs.

1429
01:27:07.254 --> 01:27:08.414
Thanks.

1430
01:27:09.557 --> 01:27:11.184
We'll be in touch.

1431
01:27:22.970 --> 01:27:27.066
So does anyone think this suspect
warrants further investigation?

1432
01:27:27.174 --> 01:27:30.109
These are copies of some
of the Zodiac letters that were sent.

1433
01:27:30.678 --> 01:27:33.977
We'd like you to take a look at them.

1434
01:27:34.081 --> 01:27:35.946
You think my brother's the Zodiac.

1435
01:27:36.050 --> 01:27:38.018
Well, we're looking at him.

1436
01:27:38.119 --> 01:27:39.484
Are you going to arrest him?

1437
01:27:39.587 --> 01:27:43.523
Mrs. Allen, we don't arrest people
just because we're interested in them.

1438
01:27:43.624 --> 01:27:45.057
Well, Leigh's always been troubled.

1439
01:27:45.159 --> 01:27:47.354
Is it true about the children?

1440
01:27:47.928 --> 01:27:49.361
Unfortunately.

1441
01:27:49.463 --> 01:27:52.057
We don't see him much anymore
since we found out.

1442
01:27:52.166 --> 01:27:54.191
What are your feelings
about Don Cheney?

1443
01:27:54.301 --> 01:27:56.599
Don Cheney? My old roommate?

1444
01:27:56.704 --> 01:27:59.673
- Was he the one who contacted you?
- That's confidential.

1445
01:27:59.774 --> 01:28:01.298
Well, Don's a very reliable guy.

1446
01:28:01.409 --> 01:28:04.469
If he were to tell you something,
I'd believe it to be true.

1447
01:28:04.578 --> 01:28:05.738
- This one.
- What about it?

1448
01:28:05.846 --> 01:28:07.973
Here, where he spells
"Christmas" with two "S's."

1449
01:28:08.082 --> 01:28:10.016
We got a Christmas card from Leigh
a couple years ago.

1450
01:28:10.117 --> 01:28:13.143
He spelled it the exact same way.
Christ-mass.

1451
01:28:13.254 --> 01:28:15.984
- Would you still have that?
- I can look for it.

1452
01:28:16.090 --> 01:28:18.183
Thank you. That'd be great.

1453
01:28:19.326 --> 01:28:21.351
Is there anything else
we can do to help?

1454
01:28:21.462 --> 01:28:23.089
The brother said
he would search Leigh's apartment

1455
01:28:23.197 --> 01:28:24.425
next time he went out of town.

1456
01:28:24.532 --> 01:28:26.762
- That gets you around a warrant.
- For the time being.

1457
01:28:26.867 --> 01:28:30.098
If we do find something,
Mulanax will go to the DA in Vallejo,

1458
01:28:30.204 --> 01:28:31.933
and we could search the place properly.

1459
01:28:32.039 --> 01:28:33.506
Now I got a chance to talk to the cop

1460
01:28:33.607 --> 01:28:36.474
who interviewed Leigh Allen
two days after the Berryessa murders.

1461
01:28:36.577 --> 01:28:38.272
Doesn't remember how he got onto him,

1462
01:28:38.379 --> 01:28:41.371
but didn't think he looked like a killer
so he didn't like him for Z.

1463
01:28:41.482 --> 01:28:44.315
- But you do?
- I wish I could've taken the guy in there.

1464
01:28:44.418 --> 01:28:47.353
Take it slow, Dave.
Try and find more stuff for Sherwood.

1465
01:28:47.455 --> 01:28:49.480
A match'll get us farther
on the warrants.

1466
01:28:49.590 --> 01:28:52.684
- Avery's on two.
- Tell him to screw.

1467
01:28:52.793 --> 01:28:57.093
You want me to communicate that
verbatim or can I spice it up a little?

1468
01:29:06.907 --> 01:29:08.340
Christ, kid.

1469
01:29:10.010 --> 01:29:10.942
Yeah.

1470
01:29:11.045 --> 01:29:13.343
- Paul, I've been thinking...
- Oh, God save us all.

1471
01:29:13.447 --> 01:29:14.812
The letter to Melvin Belli

1472
01:29:14.915 --> 01:29:17.850
was sent exactly one year
after the Lake Herman Road murder.

1473
01:29:17.952 --> 01:29:19.681
And the one to Cheri Jo Bates' father

1474
01:29:19.787 --> 01:29:22.153
was sent exactly six months
after her death.

1475
01:29:22.256 --> 01:29:24.554
- She was killed a day before Halloween.
- Yeah.

1476
01:29:24.658 --> 01:29:26.148
And you received a Halloween card...

1477
01:29:26.260 --> 01:29:28.854
You know, these are all fascinating
pieces of news, Robert,

1478
01:29:28.963 --> 01:29:30.897
it's a bit early in the day.

1479
01:29:30.998 --> 01:29:33.831
Paul, it's 11:00 and we missed Editorial.

1480
01:29:38.439 --> 01:29:40.464
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake you up.
- No, no, no.

1481
01:29:40.574 --> 01:29:41.768
- I just thought that...
- No, no, no.

1482
01:29:47.410 --> 01:29:49.742
This suspect is not your Zodiac.

1483
01:29:51.848 --> 01:29:54.373
This sample matches the canceled
checks and the application?

1484
01:29:54.484 --> 01:29:55.473
Perfectly.

1485
01:29:55.585 --> 01:29:58.782
So we've just retested the left hand.
I mean, we know he's ambidextrous.

1486
01:29:58.888 --> 01:30:02.119
In 38 years, I've never seen anyone
that ambidextrous.

1487
01:30:02.225 --> 01:30:04.716
Both hands would have commonalities.

1488
01:30:05.094 --> 01:30:06.356
I'm sorry.

1489
01:30:06.863 --> 01:30:08.592
Just not gonna work.

1490
01:30:10.533 --> 01:30:12.933
- Homicide, Toschi.
- Dave, it's Jack Mulanax.

1491
01:30:13.036 --> 01:30:15.163
Hey. Mulanax. Yeah.

1492
01:30:15.271 --> 01:30:16.670
We struck out with the judge.

1493
01:30:16.773 --> 01:30:18.400
He won't sign off on a warrant
for Allen's house.

1494
01:30:18.508 --> 01:30:20.533
- Why not?
- Said it wasn't enough.

1495
01:30:20.643 --> 01:30:22.975
Now, unless we bring him a handwriting
match or some evidence that...

1496
01:30:23.079 --> 01:30:25.445
How are we gonna get evidence
if we can't toss the house?

1497
01:30:25.548 --> 01:30:26.981
I don't know.

1498
01:30:27.550 --> 01:30:30.451
- I truly am sorry.
- No, no. Thank you, Jack.

1499
01:30:32.355 --> 01:30:33.413
What do you wanna do?

1500
01:30:33.523 --> 01:30:34.854
Don't know what I can do
without Vallejo.

1501
01:30:34.957 --> 01:30:37.790
We need Allen's right hand.
We can't get it without a warrant.

1502
01:30:37.894 --> 01:30:39.987
Are there other guys
you should be looking at?

1503
01:30:40.096 --> 01:30:42.030
Only, what?

1504
01:30:42.131 --> 01:30:44.031
Twenty-three hundred?

1505
01:30:44.133 --> 01:30:45.464
Okay, then.

1506
01:30:48.638 --> 01:30:49.969
Okay, then.

1507
01:31:17.900 --> 01:31:20.562
Paul, you wrote the Justice Department

1508
01:31:20.670 --> 01:31:24.003
asking to be put in charge
of the Zodiac investigation?

1509
01:31:26.042 --> 01:31:27.942
I merely suggested...

1510
01:31:28.044 --> 01:31:29.238
On our letterhead?

1511
01:31:29.345 --> 01:31:31.370
...that those with intimate knowledge
of the case

1512
01:31:31.481 --> 01:31:33.415
create an information clearinghouse

1513
01:31:33.516 --> 01:31:35.643
to promote an exchange
and free flow of ideas.

1514
01:31:35.751 --> 01:31:38.811
- And that you run it.
- Well, who better than me?

1515
01:31:39.889 --> 01:31:41.413
The marked man.

1516
01:31:42.158 --> 01:31:44.092
Paul, if you want to work here,
I need three things.

1517
01:31:44.193 --> 01:31:45.660
One, stop boozing.

1518
01:31:45.761 --> 01:31:48.924
Two, stop doing
whatever else it is you're doing.

1519
01:31:49.031 --> 01:31:52.523
And three, cut this nonsense out.

1520
01:31:52.635 --> 01:31:55.695
Sweetest of Templetons, if at any time

1521
01:31:55.805 --> 01:32:01.004
you feel my excellent work is no longer
in step with this trashy provincial rag,

1522
01:32:01.110 --> 01:32:02.771
I'll more than happily...

1523
01:32:02.879 --> 01:32:06.337
More than happily
decamp for greener pastures.

1524
01:32:06.449 --> 01:32:08.041
Paul, I mean it!

1525
01:32:18.261 --> 01:32:20.126
- Paul?
- Yep.

1526
01:32:20.229 --> 01:32:23.426
- What was that?
- An editorial tête-à-tête.

1527
01:32:24.600 --> 01:32:26.693
- Wanna grab a drink?
- It's 10:00 in the morning.

1528
01:32:26.802 --> 01:32:28.599
Late breakfast?

1529
01:32:29.639 --> 01:32:31.732
- Early lunch, or...
- Paul.

1530
01:32:34.243 --> 01:32:35.676
Are you okay?

1531
01:32:36.546 --> 01:32:37.570
No.

1532
01:32:41.017 --> 01:32:42.814
Thank you for asking.

1533
01:32:45.054 --> 01:32:47.181
Shorty! Let's go out for one.

1534
01:32:47.290 --> 01:32:49.281
Paul, where are you going?

1535
01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:52.918
So, you moved off my brother-in-law?

1536
01:32:53.930 --> 01:32:55.864
We couldn't get a warrant.

1537
01:32:57.533 --> 01:33:00.934
Last year we arranged for Leigh
to get help from a social worker.

1538
01:33:01.037 --> 01:33:02.664
He only went twice.

1539
01:33:02.772 --> 01:33:05.741
We saw him recently for
the first time in nine months.

1540
01:33:05.841 --> 01:33:08.969
My mother-in-law brought him by
to see the new baby.

1541
01:33:09.078 --> 01:33:12.377
After he left,
I went to see that social worker.

1542
01:33:12.481 --> 01:33:15.814
He couldn't talk about a former patient,
so I just asked him straight out

1543
01:33:15.918 --> 01:33:18.079
if he thought Leigh
was capable of killing people.

1544
01:33:18.187 --> 01:33:21.418
- Because of patient confidentiality...
- The man said yes.

1545
01:33:23.259 --> 01:33:25.420
Why hadn't you seen him
in nine months?

1546
01:33:25.528 --> 01:33:27.428
He's going to school in Santa Rosa.

1547
01:33:27.530 --> 01:33:30.863
- Santa Rosa? Where is he living?
- In his trailer.

1548
01:33:30.967 --> 01:33:32.992
- In Santa Rosa?
- Sonoma County.

1549
01:33:33.102 --> 01:33:35.297
We wouldn't have to go
through the Vallejo DA.

1550
01:33:35.404 --> 01:33:36.894
It's been 11 months
since you talked to this guy,

1551
01:33:37.006 --> 01:33:38.530
and now you wanna search his trailer?

1552
01:33:38.641 --> 01:33:40.404
If we find something, great.

1553
01:33:40.509 --> 01:33:43.672
If not, we get his prints and
handwriting samples from both hands.

1554
01:33:43.779 --> 01:33:46.145
I thought Sherwood shut you down.

1555
01:33:46.882 --> 01:33:49.350
What if I can get a second opinion?

1556
01:33:50.519 --> 01:33:52.510
I don't wanna step on Sherwood's toes.
He trained me at this.

1557
01:33:52.622 --> 01:33:55.386
Terry, all I need to know
is if the suspect is ambidextrous.

1558
01:33:55.491 --> 01:33:59.450
Could he possibly have written
those letters with his other hand?

1559
01:34:01.163 --> 01:34:02.528
Between you and me?

1560
01:34:02.632 --> 01:34:06.068
Because there are differing
schools of thought on this.

1561
01:34:07.270 --> 01:34:11.707
Get the samples of his other hand.
If he's the Zodiac, you'll get a match.

1562
01:34:11.807 --> 01:34:14.367
That's the current thinking,
according to Terry Pascoe.

1563
01:34:14.477 --> 01:34:17.742
Meanwhile, I spoke to a psychologist
who'd be willing to testify

1564
01:34:17.847 --> 01:34:20.816
that someone who undergoes
a personality change like Zodiac

1565
01:34:20.916 --> 01:34:23.851
would manifest it physically,
altering his handwriting.

1566
01:34:23.953 --> 01:34:27.548
Which is why Sherwood couldn't
get a match from Allen's samples.

1567
01:34:27.657 --> 01:34:29.887
We got Terry Pascoe,
this psychology guy,

1568
01:34:29.992 --> 01:34:31.323
coupled with Cheney...

1569
01:34:31.427 --> 01:34:32.894
It could be enough for a warrant.

1570
01:34:32.995 --> 01:34:34.121
Get Cheney on the record.

1571
01:34:34.397 --> 01:34:37.457
"And that he would call himself Zodiac."

1572
01:34:38.567 --> 01:34:39.591
Yes.

1573
01:34:39.702 --> 01:34:43.263
And you're willing to swear
to this, under oath, in Superior Court?

1574
01:34:43.372 --> 01:34:44.771
Without any hesitation.

1575
01:34:44.874 --> 01:34:47.035
Thank you very much, Mr. Cheney.
Thank you very much for your time.

1576
01:34:47.143 --> 01:34:48.132
Thank you.

1577
01:34:48.244 --> 01:34:50.041
Suspect is Arthur Leigh Allen.

1578
01:34:50.146 --> 01:34:53.877
Lives in Sunset Trailer Court
in Santa Rosa, California.

1579
01:34:53.983 --> 01:34:55.575
Physical description.

1580
01:34:55.685 --> 01:34:57.880
Allen is similar in height,
weight and build

1581
01:34:57.987 --> 01:35:01.081
to a man seen at Lake Berryessa
on the day of the stabbings.

1582
01:35:01.190 --> 01:35:03.988
I understand he doesn't look
much like the San Francisco composite.

1583
01:35:04.093 --> 01:35:05.617
True. Height and weight are sketchy,

1584
01:35:05.728 --> 01:35:07.923
but lumbering Caucasian
with a crew cut is right on.

1585
01:35:08.030 --> 01:35:10.328
We never had much confidence
in the composite from the kids.

1586
01:35:10.433 --> 01:35:12.424
The patrolman
who saw Zodiac that night

1587
01:35:12.535 --> 01:35:14.002
said he didn't look much like the sketch.

1588
01:35:14.103 --> 01:35:15.570
Military boot prints.

1589
01:35:15.671 --> 01:35:18.401
Allen was in the Navy.
Wears a size 10-and-a-half.

1590
01:35:18.507 --> 01:35:20.941
Same size as the prints
found at Berryessa.

1591
01:35:21.043 --> 01:35:22.738
What about gun?

1592
01:35:22.845 --> 01:35:27.407
Cheney says Allen owns several
firearms. We'll list them in the warrant.

1593
01:35:27.516 --> 01:35:30.280
- And the ciphers.
- Could be code training in the Navy,

1594
01:35:30.386 --> 01:35:33.082
and people have seen Allen
with ciphers in the past.

1595
01:35:33.189 --> 01:35:34.213
Really? Who?

1596
01:35:34.323 --> 01:35:37.121
That would be his sister-in-law
and a man named Phil Tucker

1597
01:35:37.226 --> 01:35:39.524
that he worked with
at a public pool in Vallejo.

1598
01:35:39.628 --> 01:35:43.086
And Phil Tucker told us about
a conversation that he had with Allen

1599
01:35:43.199 --> 01:35:45.895
about how to attach a flashlight
to the barrel of a gun.

1600
01:35:46.001 --> 01:35:49.232
That gives us two sources
on the ciphers and two on the flashlight.

1601
01:35:49.338 --> 01:35:51.329
What about his threats on children?

1602
01:35:51.440 --> 01:35:53.203
Suspect worked for elementary schools

1603
01:35:53.309 --> 01:35:56.506
and was fired for molestation
in March, April '68.

1604
01:35:56.612 --> 01:35:59.240
- Could give him motive.
- At the very least, it's home turf.

1605
01:35:59.348 --> 01:36:01.407
He'd have knowledge of bus routes,

1606
01:36:01.517 --> 01:36:03.951
which the two major threats
centered around.

1607
01:36:04.053 --> 01:36:05.748
What about the bomb?

1608
01:36:07.189 --> 01:36:09.157
Allen works as a chemist.

1609
01:36:09.258 --> 01:36:10.691
Take him through the geography.

1610
01:36:10.793 --> 01:36:12.260
Vallejo murders.

1611
01:36:12.361 --> 01:36:15.853
Allen lives in Vallejo
with his mother in her basement.

1612
01:36:15.965 --> 01:36:19.128
Berryessa murder. On the day
that the two kids were stabbed

1613
01:36:19.235 --> 01:36:21.897
his neighbor saw bloody knives
in his truck

1614
01:36:22.004 --> 01:36:24.905
which he claimed were used
to kill a chicken.

1615
01:36:25.007 --> 01:36:26.838
Does he have any alibis?

1616
01:36:26.942 --> 01:36:29.604
He claimed he did, but he's been unable
to produce the names

1617
01:36:29.712 --> 01:36:32.977
of the couple he supposedly met
on the day of Berryessa.

1618
01:36:33.082 --> 01:36:35.448
The bottom line is that Allen
can't alibi up on anything.

1619
01:36:35.551 --> 01:36:37.348
Riverside, Vallejo, the lake or us.

1620
01:36:37.453 --> 01:36:39.648
- You want to tell me about the name?
- What name?

1621
01:36:39.755 --> 01:36:40.847
Zodiac.

1622
01:36:40.956 --> 01:36:44.824
Allen wears a watch that bears
both the word and crosshair symbol.

1623
01:36:44.927 --> 01:36:46.292
And he mentioned Zodiac to Cheney

1624
01:36:46.395 --> 01:36:48.920
a year and a half
before it appeared in any letter.

1625
01:36:52.134 --> 01:36:54.568
- John...
- That's pretty good, guys.

1626
01:36:54.670 --> 01:36:57.639
- We think so, too.
- Let's take it to a judge.

1627
01:37:17.860 --> 01:37:19.122
Mr. Allen?

1628
01:37:19.228 --> 01:37:21.219
This is the
Santa Rosa Police Department.

1629
01:37:21.330 --> 01:37:24.128
We have a warrant
to search your residence.

1630
01:37:35.177 --> 01:37:36.303
Hello?

1631
01:37:45.054 --> 01:37:47.284
I'll check with the neighbors.

1632
01:37:48.591 --> 01:37:49.615
Close the door.

1633
01:37:49.725 --> 01:37:52.751
Close the door,
there's rodents running around.

1634
01:38:05.140 --> 01:38:07.631
Neighbor said he tore out of here
about a half-hour ago.

1635
01:38:07.743 --> 01:38:12.043
- You think somebody tipped him?
- We're not leaving till he comes back.

1636
01:38:17.920 --> 01:38:19.649
I'll check the back.

1637
01:38:32.401 --> 01:38:33.390
Jesus.

1638
01:38:33.502 --> 01:38:35.094
- What?
- Squirrels.

1639
01:38:37.273 --> 01:38:39.207
Piece of work, this guy.

1640
01:38:46.148 --> 01:38:48.810
Not one, but two blue windbreakers.

1641
01:38:48.918 --> 01:38:52.581
- Like the Stine scene?
- We'll have those checked for blood.

1642
01:38:53.088 --> 01:38:55.989
And a pair of black gloves.

1643
01:38:57.359 --> 01:39:00.624
Men's seven,
just like the ones we found in the cab.

1644
01:39:00.729 --> 01:39:03.254
Well, he's got the same size shoes
and gloves as Z.

1645
01:39:03.365 --> 01:39:05.799
Probably just a coincidence.

1646
01:39:05.901 --> 01:39:09.735
Dave, I got a gun.
Check that. Two guns.

1647
01:39:10.940 --> 01:39:14.171
They're both .22s.
One automatic, one revolver.

1648
01:39:14.276 --> 01:39:15.766
Well, that's interesting.

1649
01:39:15.878 --> 01:39:19.006
Because he happens to have
an M-1 rifle here in the closet.

1650
01:39:19.114 --> 01:39:21.708
For little darlings bouncing off buses.

1651
01:39:23.218 --> 01:39:24.708
Someone's here.

1652
01:39:31.694 --> 01:39:34.094
Hello, Arthur. Remember us?

1653
01:39:56.685 --> 01:39:57.743
No.

1654
01:39:57.853 --> 01:39:58.911
On the handwriting?

1655
01:39:59.021 --> 01:40:02.513
Ballistics, no match.
Prints, no match. Writing, no match.

1656
01:40:02.625 --> 01:40:04.354
On both hands, right?

1657
01:40:04.460 --> 01:40:06.257
Because we got handwriting
from both his hands.

1658
01:40:06.362 --> 01:40:07.693
And neither hand matches.

1659
01:40:07.796 --> 01:40:09.423
Forget Sherwood.
Let's get another opinion.

1660
01:40:09.531 --> 01:40:11.522
Fellas, he's not your guy.

1661
01:40:18.240 --> 01:40:19.434
Damn it.

1662
01:40:26.615 --> 01:40:27.639
Hey.

1663
01:40:28.517 --> 01:40:31.077
What do you want? Time off?

1664
01:40:33.288 --> 01:40:34.414
A hug?

1665
01:40:35.324 --> 01:40:37.258
Do you know what
the worst part of this is?

1666
01:40:37.359 --> 01:40:39.259
I can't tell if I wanted it
to be Allen so bad

1667
01:40:39.361 --> 01:40:42.626
because I actually thought it was him,
or I just want all this to be over.

1668
01:40:42.731 --> 01:40:44.631
It's because you thought it was him.

1669
01:40:44.733 --> 01:40:46.223
And I did, too.

1670
01:40:49.071 --> 01:40:50.470
You know what? Take some time off.

1671
01:40:50.572 --> 01:40:53.837
Spend some time with your wife
and the kids.

1672
01:40:53.942 --> 01:40:56.467
Go to Candlestick. See a movie.

1673
01:40:57.813 --> 01:41:03.115
"To the city of San Francisco,
I will enjoy killing one person every day

1674
01:41:03.218 --> 01:41:05.618
"until you pay me $100,000.

1675
01:41:06.622 --> 01:41:09.318
"If you agree, say so tomorrow morning

1676
01:41:10.159 --> 01:41:13.094
"in the personal column
San Francisco Chronicle,

1677
01:41:13.195 --> 01:41:15.163
"and I will set up meeting.

1678
01:41:15.264 --> 01:41:16.856
"If I do not hear from you,

1679
01:41:16.965 --> 01:41:19.934
"it will be my next pleasure
to kill a Catholic priest or a...

1680
01:41:23.372 --> 01:41:24.805
"...Scorpio."

1681
01:41:27.209 --> 01:41:28.676
Who's out of their minds?

1682
01:41:28.777 --> 01:41:30.836
I've got to get out of here.

1683
01:41:30.946 --> 01:41:34.211
Where the hell does he expect me
to find $100,000?

1684
01:41:34.316 --> 01:41:36.682
You're not thinking of paying him,
are you, Mr. Mayor?

1685
01:41:36.785 --> 01:41:41.085
The city of San Francisco does not
pay criminals not to commit a crime.

1686
01:42:04.046 --> 01:42:06.514
The killer gets shot in the chest.

1687
01:42:06.615 --> 01:42:08.879
That's how it ends.

1688
01:42:09.351 --> 01:42:10.943
Do I know you?

1689
01:42:11.053 --> 01:42:13.817
I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the Chronicle with Paul Avery.

1690
01:42:13.922 --> 01:42:15.480
Dave Toschi. Nice to meet you.

1691
01:42:15.591 --> 01:42:18.082
Dave! That Harry Callahan
did a hell of a job with your case.

1692
01:42:18.193 --> 01:42:20.787
Yeah. No need for due process, right?

1693
01:42:25.134 --> 01:42:27.125
- What do you do at the Chronicle?
- I'm a cartoonist.

1694
01:42:27.236 --> 01:42:28.533
That's nice.

1695
01:42:28.637 --> 01:42:30.537
You're gonna catch him.

1696
01:42:32.207 --> 01:42:35.005
Pal, they're already
making movies about it.

1697
01:42:42.785 --> 01:42:45.720
We today have concluded
an agreement

1698
01:42:45.821 --> 01:42:49.416
to end the war and bring peace
with honor in Vietnam.

1699
01:42:49.525 --> 01:42:52.585
...Charles Manson for
the Tate-La Bianca mass murders...

1700
01:42:52.694 --> 01:42:54.958
Guilty in the Chowchilla
kidnapping case.

1701
01:42:55.063 --> 01:42:57.327
In the murder trial of one...

1702
01:42:57.432 --> 01:42:59.229
Chairman Mao died today...

1703
01:42:59.334 --> 01:43:01.700
...an absolute pardon
unto Richard Nixon...

1704
01:43:01.804 --> 01:43:04.773
- No, I'm not a crook...
- ...Generation of hostility...

1705
01:43:06.975 --> 01:43:09.944
...has now led to the death
of 50,000 Americans

1706
01:43:10.045 --> 01:43:12.980
and several
hundred thousand Vietnamese...

1707
01:43:13.081 --> 01:43:15.777
Patricia Hearst is kidnapped
by the Symbionese Liberation Army...

1708
01:43:15.884 --> 01:43:19.217
All of us should stand up together
and say, "No more."

1709
01:43:20.823 --> 01:43:23.451
Your Declaration of Independence
spreads that...

1710
01:43:23.559 --> 01:43:26.153
Americans admire
the United Kingdom...

1711
01:43:26.261 --> 01:43:28.286
Mr. Hoffa has disappeared.

1712
01:43:28.397 --> 01:43:31.889
If we despise our own government...

1713
01:43:32.000 --> 01:43:35.163
...that the police have captured a man

1714
01:43:35.270 --> 01:43:36.897
whom they believe
to be the "Son of Sam..."

1715
01:43:52.387 --> 01:43:54.514
Hi. We haven't met.

1716
01:43:54.623 --> 01:43:56.591
I'm Robert Graysmith.

1717
01:43:56.692 --> 01:43:58.557
I'm Duffy Jennings.

1718
01:43:58.660 --> 01:44:01.754
- Nice to meet you.
- Good to meet you, man.

1719
01:44:01.864 --> 01:44:02.956
You got a great desk.

1720
01:44:03.065 --> 01:44:05.090
Guy who used to work here
was a great reporter.

1721
01:44:05.200 --> 01:44:06.462
Oh, yeah. Oh, I'm sure he was.

1722
01:44:06.568 --> 01:44:09.036
I mean, it's a honor
to leave the Chronicle

1723
01:44:09.137 --> 01:44:11.935
and go work for the Sacramento Bee.

1724
01:44:12.040 --> 01:44:14.201
Dare to dream, right, Robert?

1725
01:44:17.880 --> 01:44:20.747
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.

1726
01:44:20.849 --> 01:44:22.942
I'm just right down there
at the Art department

1727
01:44:23.051 --> 01:44:25.519
- if you need anything, Duffy.
- Yeah.

1728
01:44:29.057 --> 01:44:31.726
- You sure you don't want the car, Bill?
- It's your turn.

1729
01:44:31.827 --> 01:44:34.990
You could just drop me off at my place
and take the car.

1730
01:44:35.097 --> 01:44:37.031
You should keep the car.

1731
01:44:37.799 --> 01:44:38.857
Yeah?

1732
01:44:39.434 --> 01:44:41.493
I'm not coming in tomorrow.

1733
01:44:43.472 --> 01:44:44.962
Why? What's up?

1734
01:44:46.208 --> 01:44:47.436
I'm done.

1735
01:44:48.977 --> 01:44:50.911
I put in for a transfer.

1736
01:44:56.952 --> 01:44:58.180
Where?

1737
01:44:58.620 --> 01:45:00.212
Looking at Fraud.

1738
01:45:02.457 --> 01:45:04.516
I can't be on call anymore.

1739
01:45:07.329 --> 01:45:09.593
I wanna see these kids grow up.

1740
01:45:10.766 --> 01:45:12.996
Hey, good for you, Bill.

1741
01:45:14.903 --> 01:45:17.394
- You'll be okay.
- Yeah. I'll be fine.

1742
01:45:19.474 --> 01:45:20.498
Hey,

1743
01:45:21.610 --> 01:45:25.011
I'm not leaving you
holding the bag on anything, am I?

1744
01:45:26.715 --> 01:45:27.739
No.

1745
01:45:30.118 --> 01:45:31.176
Okay.

1746
01:45:31.853 --> 01:45:33.548
Hey, you know what?

1747
01:45:34.189 --> 01:45:38.387
Maybe you'll have a chance
to try your Japanese food, the raw stuff.

1748
01:45:39.394 --> 01:45:40.452
Yeah.

1749
01:46:12.461 --> 01:46:14.156
I'm not Paul Avery.

1750
01:46:17.065 --> 01:46:20.000
The boys need to be tucked in, please,
and the baby needs changing.

1751
01:46:20.102 --> 01:46:22.400
- I'll flip you for it.
- You wish.

1752
01:46:25.874 --> 01:46:28.536
Nobody has more Zodiac crap
than you do.

1753
01:47:13.255 --> 01:47:15.450
- Are you kidding me?
- Hi, Paul.

1754
01:47:17.225 --> 01:47:19.887
Permission to come aboard.
It's right there.

1755
01:47:19.995 --> 01:47:22.463
Anyway, you got shoes on.
This is perfect right here.

1756
01:47:22.564 --> 01:47:24.464
- That's the one.
- Okay.

1757
01:47:26.201 --> 01:47:28.999
- See that? Mesmerizing.
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1758
01:47:29.104 --> 01:47:31.732
My own kids
would kill me for one of those.

1759
01:47:33.608 --> 01:47:35.838
- How are you?
- Fantastic.

1760
01:47:35.944 --> 01:47:38.071
I mean, admittedly,

1761
01:47:38.180 --> 01:47:40.512
the Bee ain't exactly
the Chron, but fuck it, right?

1762
01:47:40.615 --> 01:47:43.516
Do you want a drink?
I don't have anything blue, but I got...

1763
01:47:43.618 --> 01:47:45.586
Don't worry about that.
Don't worry about it.

1764
01:47:45.687 --> 01:47:49.248
It's no bother at all.
Nobody comes by from the old days.

1765
01:47:49.658 --> 01:47:50.682
Cheers.

1766
01:47:51.460 --> 01:47:53.587
To your health and mine.

1767
01:47:55.530 --> 01:47:56.895
Mostly mine.

1768
01:48:02.104 --> 01:48:03.594
So,

1769
01:48:05.807 --> 01:48:07.138
what's new?

1770
01:48:09.177 --> 01:48:11.077
- I've been thinking.
- Yeah.

1771
01:48:11.179 --> 01:48:12.305
Somebody should write a book.

1772
01:48:12.414 --> 01:48:15.349
Somebody should write a fucking book,
that's for sure.

1773
01:48:15.450 --> 01:48:17.577
- About what?
- About Zodiac.

1774
01:48:19.221 --> 01:48:20.620
It's not new.

1775
01:48:20.722 --> 01:48:25.352
I've been thinking that
if you put all the information together,

1776
01:48:25.460 --> 01:48:27.018
maybe you could jog something loose.

1777
01:48:27.129 --> 01:48:29.620
And then I was thinking that
nobody knows the case better than you.

1778
01:48:29.731 --> 01:48:30.755
Yeah. That's true.

1779
01:48:30.866 --> 01:48:33.858
You know all the players,
and you have all the files.

1780
01:48:33.969 --> 01:48:35.266
Lost them.

1781
01:48:35.604 --> 01:48:36.662
You lost them?

1782
01:48:36.771 --> 01:48:40.036
Or I tossed them. I don't know.
I moved onto a boat.

1783
01:48:40.475 --> 01:48:42.534
You know that we work
in the daily business, right?

1784
01:48:42.644 --> 01:48:43.906
As in, today.

1785
01:48:44.012 --> 01:48:46.776
What do you think
we were doing back then?

1786
01:48:47.782 --> 01:48:49.909
Do you know that more people die
in the East Bay commute

1787
01:48:50.018 --> 01:48:52.316
every three months
than that idiot ever killed?

1788
01:48:52.420 --> 01:48:53.580
He offed a few citizens,

1789
01:48:53.688 --> 01:48:57.021
he wrote a few letters,
and he faded into a footnote.

1790
01:49:02.531 --> 01:49:05.523
Not that I haven't been sitting here idly

1791
01:49:05.634 --> 01:49:09.593
waiting for you to drop by
and reinvigorate my sense of purpose.

1792
01:49:11.940 --> 01:49:15.068
It was four years ago. Let it fucking go.

1793
01:49:15.177 --> 01:49:17.873
You're wrong. It was important.

1794
01:49:19.147 --> 01:49:21.638
Then, what did you ever do about it?

1795
01:49:22.517 --> 01:49:24.644
If it was so fucking important,
what did you ever do?

1796
01:49:24.753 --> 01:49:27.586
You hovered over my desk,
you stole from wastebaskets.

1797
01:49:27.689 --> 01:49:29.316
Am I being unkind?

1798
01:49:30.492 --> 01:49:33.757
Oh, that's right, I forgot.
You went to the library.

1799
01:49:36.565 --> 01:49:38.533
I'm sorry I bothered you.

1800
01:50:00.655 --> 01:50:02.680
- Hey, hi.
- Hi.

1801
01:50:02.791 --> 01:50:05.225
- Where you been?
- The library.

1802
01:50:36.891 --> 01:50:38.188
Thank you!

1803
01:50:53.942 --> 01:50:57.309
- Inspector Toschi?
- Yeah? One moment, please.

1804
01:51:01.683 --> 01:51:02.877
- Hi.
- Hi.

1805
01:51:04.185 --> 01:51:06.176
We met at the movies once.

1806
01:51:06.688 --> 01:51:08.053
It must have been magical.

1807
01:51:08.156 --> 01:51:09.885
I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the Chronicle.

1808
01:51:09.991 --> 01:51:12.756
I was wondering if I could buy you lunch.

1809
01:51:14.496 --> 01:51:16.157
Sure, why not?

1810
01:51:16.264 --> 01:51:18.630
So, you're a friend of Paul Avery's?

1811
01:51:18.733 --> 01:51:21.133
He's actually the reason I'm here.

1812
01:51:22.871 --> 01:51:25.237
I wanted to ask you about Zodiac.

1813
01:51:25.707 --> 01:51:28.938
Well, I appreciate the interest,
but we don't discuss open cases.

1814
01:51:29.044 --> 01:51:31.569
Oh, well, what's going on with it,
day to day?

1815
01:51:31.680 --> 01:51:33.341
We're actively pursuing all leads.

1816
01:51:33.448 --> 01:51:36.008
And you're the only one on it, right?

1817
01:51:37.185 --> 01:51:38.652
Mr. Graysmith,

1818
01:51:39.788 --> 01:51:41.756
Zodiac hasn't written in three years.

1819
01:51:41.856 --> 01:51:44.586
You know how many murders
we've had in San Francisco since then?

1820
01:51:44.693 --> 01:51:46.183
- No.
- Over 200.

1821
01:51:46.294 --> 01:51:49.593
That's a lot of dead people
and grieving families that need our help.

1822
01:51:49.698 --> 01:51:51.290
So, nobody cares.

1823
01:51:51.433 --> 01:51:53.867
Excuse me? I care.

1824
01:51:56.571 --> 01:51:58.835
Okay. Can I show you something?

1825
01:52:01.743 --> 01:52:04.906
I've been doing research
on the first cipher.

1826
01:52:05.013 --> 01:52:06.776
Everything an amateur
would need to create it

1827
01:52:06.881 --> 01:52:09.850
can be found in these books.

1828
01:52:09.951 --> 01:52:13.284
Now, I started thinking
that if you can track these books,

1829
01:52:13.388 --> 01:52:15.788
then maybe you can track the man.

1830
01:52:16.324 --> 01:52:19.157
So, I remember you thought
that Zodiac was military,

1831
01:52:19.260 --> 01:52:22.923
so I went to every base library
and I got a list of every person

1832
01:52:23.031 --> 01:52:26.967
who's ever checked out these books
and that's when I found this.

1833
01:52:31.706 --> 01:52:34.197
- Missing.
- It means they were stolen.

1834
01:52:35.009 --> 01:52:38.570
So, almost every book on ciphers
was stolen from the Presidio Library?

1835
01:52:38.680 --> 01:52:41.274
And the Oakland Army Terminal Library.

1836
01:52:44.085 --> 01:52:48.522
Somebody didn't want a record
of ever having checked out these books.

1837
01:52:48.623 --> 01:52:50.250
Who are you again?

1838
01:52:52.360 --> 01:52:53.987
I just wanna help.

1839
01:52:57.198 --> 01:52:59.462
I can't allow you to help.

1840
01:52:59.567 --> 01:53:01.330
I can't discuss the case with you.

1841
01:53:01.436 --> 01:53:03.870
I can't give you information,
and I certainly couldn't tell you

1842
01:53:03.972 --> 01:53:06.167
to go see Ken Narlow in Napa.

1843
01:53:06.741 --> 01:53:08.106
N-A-R-L-O-W.

1844
01:53:18.119 --> 01:53:22.783
I'm sorry, Mr. Graysmith,
but we don't cooperate with writers.

1845
01:53:22.891 --> 01:53:25.655
Well, I'm not a writer, I'm a cartoonist.

1846
01:53:26.594 --> 01:53:28.789
- And Dave Toschi sent you?
- Yes.

1847
01:53:28.897 --> 01:53:30.865
- Why?
- Maybe he...

1848
01:53:30.965 --> 01:53:33.763
Maybe he thought
that I could do some good.

1849
01:53:34.502 --> 01:53:38.666
- What are you, some kind of boy scout?
- Eagle Scout, actually, first class.

1850
01:53:39.641 --> 01:53:42.804
Well, if you wanna do this,
don't let me stop you.

1851
01:53:44.112 --> 01:53:46.171
Better start with Vallejo, Jack Mulanax.

1852
01:53:47.148 --> 01:53:49.548
I understand what you're trying to do.

1853
01:53:49.651 --> 01:53:51.846
But this is an open police investigation.

1854
01:53:51.953 --> 01:53:54.046
I'm a friend of Dave Toschi's.

1855
01:53:54.155 --> 01:53:57.420
And he said
that you might be able to help.

1856
01:53:57.525 --> 01:54:00.426
I mean, the case is dead.
Zodiac's long gone.

1857
01:54:01.362 --> 01:54:03.523
He's yesterday's news, right?

1858
01:54:04.599 --> 01:54:06.362
That's what they say.

1859
01:54:07.302 --> 01:54:09.133
So, what's the harm?

1860
01:54:09.237 --> 01:54:10.670
No pens, no paper.

1861
01:54:11.239 --> 01:54:13.901
Anything that you see that's relevant,
you got to remember in your head.

1862
01:54:14.008 --> 01:54:15.066
Okay.

1863
01:54:17.312 --> 01:54:18.609
Okay, here we go.

1864
01:54:18.713 --> 01:54:20.772
- Which one?
- All of them.

1865
01:54:20.882 --> 01:54:23.578
And there's more in the next room.
They're all marked with these numbers.

1866
01:54:23.685 --> 01:54:24.879
243-146.

1867
01:54:24.986 --> 01:54:26.817
You don't smoke, do you?

1868
01:54:26.921 --> 01:54:29.014
Once. In high school.

1869
01:54:32.427 --> 01:54:33.792
What's this?

1870
01:54:34.729 --> 01:54:36.026
Thank you.

1871
01:55:04.259 --> 01:55:06.250
Man, you really creeped us out.

1872
01:55:12.133 --> 01:55:14.124
"Nine millimeter.

1873
01:55:15.703 --> 01:55:18.228
"Said nothing and began firing."

1874
01:55:27.048 --> 01:55:28.345
"Most Dangerous Game.

1875
01:55:28.449 --> 01:55:31.213
"Do not eliminate this suspect
because of handwriting.

1876
01:55:31.319 --> 01:55:33.412
"Not because of handwriting.

1877
01:55:33.988 --> 01:55:35.956
"Darlene's sister, Linda.

1878
01:55:36.057 --> 01:55:38.719
"It was all just deep breathing. George.

1879
01:55:39.360 --> 01:55:42.124
"It was a strange man. George.
Strange man."

1880
01:55:43.097 --> 01:55:44.724
Thank you so much.

1881
01:55:46.634 --> 01:55:48.625
Oh, briefcase. Oh, thanks.

1882
01:55:51.339 --> 01:55:53.864
- Hey, Jack.
- Hey, Bawart.

1883
01:55:53.975 --> 01:55:55.806
- Who's that?
- That's Graysmith.

1884
01:55:55.910 --> 01:55:59.175
Some cartoonist.
Thinks he's gonna solve the Zodiac.

1885
01:56:00.882 --> 01:56:02.179
Well, good for him.

1886
01:56:32.647 --> 01:56:34.911
- Thank you for meeting me, Inspector.
- No. We're not meeting, Robert.

1887
01:56:35.016 --> 01:56:36.540
We're just two guys
who happen to be sitting

1888
01:56:36.651 --> 01:56:37.811
on the same bench at the same time.

1889
01:56:37.919 --> 01:56:40.319
I've got five minutes.
I've got to get back to the Hall.

1890
01:56:40.421 --> 01:56:43.151
Okay. As far as you know,
did anyone ever get in touch

1891
01:56:43.257 --> 01:56:44.952
with Mike Mageau
during your investigation

1892
01:56:45.059 --> 01:56:47.527
- and show him suspect photos?
- Why?

1893
01:56:47.629 --> 01:56:50.063
Well, he's the only surviving victim
who ever saw Zodiac without a mask.

1894
01:56:50.164 --> 01:56:51.495
No, I mean, why are you asking me?

1895
01:56:51.599 --> 01:56:53.464
Mageau and Darlene,
that's Vallejo's case.

1896
01:56:53.568 --> 01:56:56.332
Paul Stine is mine.
You've got four minutes now.

1897
01:56:56.437 --> 01:56:58.735
Darlene Ferrin was being followed.

1898
01:56:58.840 --> 01:57:00.603
Now, I know Mulanax says
that they already found this guy,

1899
01:57:00.708 --> 01:57:01.697
a George Waters?

1900
01:57:01.809 --> 01:57:03.606
But he also said
that she had a lot of admirers

1901
01:57:03.711 --> 01:57:05.338
who would come to
the restaurant where she worked.

1902
01:57:05.446 --> 01:57:07.038
- She was popular.
- Very.

1903
01:57:07.148 --> 01:57:08.775
Yeah. So...

1904
01:57:08.883 --> 01:57:10.817
She and her husband,
they move into their new house,

1905
01:57:10.918 --> 01:57:12.545
and one night they throw
this painting party.

1906
01:57:12.654 --> 01:57:13.746
And what's a painting party?

1907
01:57:13.855 --> 01:57:15.823
It's a party where people come
and help you paint.

1908
01:57:15.923 --> 01:57:17.015
Sounds like a terrible party.

1909
01:57:17.125 --> 01:57:20.891
Well, supposedly,
somebody who's not Waters shows up.

1910
01:57:20.995 --> 01:57:22.860
And Darlene is terrified of him.

1911
01:57:22.964 --> 01:57:24.693
So you think that Darlene knew Zodiac?

1912
01:57:24.799 --> 01:57:29.259
And if Zodiac knew Darlene,
then maybe Mageau knows Zodiac.

1913
01:57:29.370 --> 01:57:31.201
Maybe. But Mageau's gone.

1914
01:57:31.305 --> 01:57:32.897
So if you wanna connect
Darlene to Zodiac,

1915
01:57:33.007 --> 01:57:34.406
you're gonna have to find another way.

1916
01:57:34.509 --> 01:57:35.840
I have another way.

1917
01:57:35.943 --> 01:57:37.535
Phone calls the night
of Darlene's murder.

1918
01:57:37.645 --> 01:57:40.739
- Yeah, Zodiac called the police.
- No, Dave, there were four other calls.

1919
01:57:40.848 --> 01:57:43.146
There were two to Darlene's house,
one to Darlene's brother-in-law,

1920
01:57:43.251 --> 01:57:45.549
and one to Darlene's father-in-law.
Just heavy breathing.

1921
01:57:45.653 --> 01:57:47.484
They started around 1:30 a.m.,

1922
01:57:47.588 --> 01:57:51.251
and this was before anyone in the family
knew that Darlene had been shot.

1923
01:57:51.359 --> 01:57:53.452
- This was in the Vallejo files?
- Yeah.

1924
01:57:53.561 --> 01:57:54.585
God damn it.

1925
01:57:54.696 --> 01:57:56.425
It's got to be more
than just a coincidence, right?

1926
01:57:56.531 --> 01:57:59.398
I mean, somebody doesn't just randomly
prank phone call a victim's entire family

1927
01:57:59.500 --> 01:58:01.525
90 minutes after they were shot.

1928
01:58:01.636 --> 01:58:03.695
So, either Zodiac shoots
a random couple,

1929
01:58:03.805 --> 01:58:05.295
then he recognizes Darlene...

1930
01:58:05.406 --> 01:58:07.397
Or Darlene was shot on purpose.

1931
01:58:07.508 --> 01:58:10.705
Either way,
Zodiac had to have known Darlene.

1932
01:58:12.613 --> 01:58:14.342
That's good, Robert.

1933
01:58:14.849 --> 01:58:18.046
So, I can't find Mageau,
so maybe I can find Darlene's sister.

1934
01:58:18.152 --> 01:58:20.052
And maybe she can tell me
who this mystery man is.

1935
01:58:20.154 --> 01:58:22.952
Try that. I've got to go. She's very cute.

1936
01:58:26.861 --> 01:58:28.385
You know,

1937
01:58:28.496 --> 01:58:31.829
it's interesting that you should mention
Zodiac calling people at home.

1938
01:58:31.933 --> 01:58:33.366
He did that in San Francisco once.

1939
01:58:33.468 --> 01:58:34.958
What? Who did he call?

1940
01:58:35.069 --> 01:58:38.129
I can't tell you.
That's privileged information.

1941
01:58:38.773 --> 01:58:40.934
But maybe Melvin Belli could.

1942
01:58:43.611 --> 01:58:45.135
Melvin Belli.

1943
01:58:46.080 --> 01:58:48.344
How do I get to Melvin Belli?

1944
01:58:48.449 --> 01:58:51.441
- He should be along soon.
- Oh, that's all right.

1945
01:58:51.552 --> 01:58:53.918
I've really...
I've only been waiting two hours, so...

1946
01:58:54.021 --> 01:58:55.852
He's usually not this late.

1947
01:58:55.957 --> 01:58:58.721
Oh, cookies. Thank you.
These look great.

1948
01:58:59.560 --> 01:59:03.462
- You are here on business?
- I'm writing a book about the Zodiac.

1949
01:59:03.564 --> 01:59:06.499
I remember that. I spoke to him.

1950
01:59:06.601 --> 01:59:11.197
- You mean to Mr. Belli about the case?
- No, to the Zodiac when he called.

1951
01:59:11.305 --> 01:59:14.604
He said he had to kill
because it was his birthday.

1952
01:59:14.709 --> 01:59:17.940
He said it... Wait.
He said it was his birthday?

1953
01:59:18.045 --> 01:59:20.570
Yes. You want something to drink?

1954
01:59:21.616 --> 01:59:25.609
- When was this?
- Oh, so many years ago.

1955
01:59:27.321 --> 01:59:29.881
Mr. Belli was away for Christmas.

1956
01:59:29.991 --> 01:59:31.219
Gone for a week.

1957
01:59:31.325 --> 01:59:33.657
The Zodiac called,
wanting to talk to him.

1958
01:59:33.761 --> 01:59:35.456
I said, "He is not here."

1959
01:59:35.563 --> 01:59:38.464
He said, "I have to kill.
Today is my birthday."

1960
01:59:38.566 --> 01:59:40.500
And then he hangs up.

1961
01:59:40.601 --> 01:59:42.091
Then the letter arrived.

1962
01:59:42.203 --> 01:59:46.230
So, the call came
before the letter of December 20th.

1963
01:59:46.340 --> 01:59:48.274
Mr. Belli was gone for a week?

1964
01:59:48.376 --> 01:59:52.107
He came back on Christmas.
Not a good day to work.

1965
01:59:52.213 --> 01:59:54.147
So, he left on the 18th.

1966
01:59:55.349 --> 01:59:56.816
Is that helpful?

1967
01:59:56.918 --> 01:59:58.351
She said it was his birthday.

1968
01:59:58.452 --> 02:00:02.252
Well, you'd have to confirm that,
now wouldn't you?

1969
02:00:02.356 --> 02:00:03.755
How?

1970
02:00:03.858 --> 02:00:06.952
Well, I never spoke to her,
but maybe my partner did.

1971
02:00:07.061 --> 02:00:09.894
- How do I get a hold of him?
- You don't. Bill wanted out of this.

1972
02:00:09.997 --> 02:00:12.261
As far as I'm concerned,
he should stay out.

1973
02:00:12.366 --> 02:00:13.628
How do I confirm it?

1974
02:00:13.734 --> 02:00:16.259
Well, if my partner
did talk to someone from Justice,

1975
02:00:16.370 --> 02:00:17.928
then they would've had
to put that in a report.

1976
02:00:18.039 --> 02:00:20.337
That's standard procedure.

1977
02:00:20.441 --> 02:00:22.500
- Okay.
- Mel Nicolai.

1978
02:00:22.610 --> 02:00:24.544
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

1979
02:00:24.645 --> 02:00:26.806
I just need to confirm a date.

1980
02:00:26.914 --> 02:00:28.245
- Mr. Graysmith...
- I've narrowed it down

1981
02:00:28.349 --> 02:00:30.613
between the 18th and the 20th
of December, and I just need...

1982
02:00:30.718 --> 02:00:34.017
Okay, I'll play.
Let's say this phone call did take place.

1983
02:00:34.121 --> 02:00:35.554
Let's say it really was Zodiac.

1984
02:00:35.656 --> 02:00:38.420
Why would he volunteer
the day he was born?

1985
02:00:38.526 --> 02:00:40.653
Plus, nobody died on December 18th,

1986
02:00:40.761 --> 02:00:43.559
just like nobody died over the weekend
when he was gonna kill a dozen people,

1987
02:00:43.664 --> 02:00:45.996
or when he was gonna
shoot school kids or blow up buses.

1988
02:00:46.100 --> 02:00:47.465
He's a liar, Mr. Graysmith.

1989
02:00:47.568 --> 02:00:49.229
What if he made a mistake?

1990
02:00:49.337 --> 02:00:51.362
What if he wasn't lying?
What if it was him on the phone?

1991
02:00:51.472 --> 02:00:53.838
He didn't expect to pick it up,
a nice person to pick up.

1992
02:00:53.941 --> 02:00:55.272
What if? What if? What if?

1993
02:00:55.376 --> 02:00:58.709
Look, off the record,
Bill Armstrong checked this out.

1994
02:00:58.813 --> 02:01:01.407
We took this very seriously.

1995
02:01:01.515 --> 02:01:04.746
None of the suspects had the
same birthday as this phantom caller.

1996
02:01:04.852 --> 02:01:07.013
Bill Armstrong.

1997
02:01:12.593 --> 02:01:14.561
Can I give you a piece of advice?

1998
02:01:14.662 --> 02:01:16.220
You're looking in the wrong place.

1999
02:01:16.330 --> 02:01:19.356
Handwriting, fingerprints,
that's what this whole thing's about.

2000
02:01:19.467 --> 02:01:20.832
Stick to the evidence.

2001
02:01:21.869 --> 02:01:22.893
Hi.

2002
02:01:31.212 --> 02:01:34.340
- Hey. How was your day?
- Long.

2003
02:01:39.787 --> 02:01:41.186
Who's Sherwood Morrill?

2004
02:01:41.289 --> 02:01:44.053
He's a handwriting expert
in Sacramento.

2005
02:01:44.158 --> 02:01:45.250
He called.

2006
02:01:45.359 --> 02:01:47.452
He said he can meet you
tomorrow morning at 7:00.

2007
02:01:47.561 --> 02:01:48.823
Oh, great.

2008
02:01:48.930 --> 02:01:51.763
- So you're taking off work?
- Just an hour.

2009
02:01:53.567 --> 02:01:55.660
Sacramento's two hours away.

2010
02:01:56.804 --> 02:01:58.396
- Really?
- Yes.

2011
02:01:59.173 --> 02:02:00.697
What's this?

2012
02:02:00.808 --> 02:02:03.436
Oh, that's that article.

2013
02:02:03.544 --> 02:02:07.105
"Robert Graysmith has quietly been
shopping his book about the Zodiac."

2014
02:02:07.214 --> 02:02:08.306
Yeah.

2015
02:02:08.416 --> 02:02:11.044
It talks all about you
researching Zodiac.

2016
02:02:11.152 --> 02:02:12.551
Well, that's what the article's about.

2017
02:02:12.653 --> 02:02:15.087
I'm not so sure that's something
we want people to know about.

2018
02:02:15.189 --> 02:02:16.247
Why? Are you embarrassed?

2019
02:02:16.357 --> 02:02:19.520
Robert, what's the one thing
we know about Zodiac?

2020
02:02:20.194 --> 02:02:21.388
He reads the Chronicle.

2021
02:02:21.495 --> 02:02:23.986
Yeah, but he's never
gonna read Herb Caen.

2022
02:02:28.669 --> 02:02:30.967
- Hello.
- Mr. Graysmith?

2023
02:02:31.072 --> 02:02:33.632
The Robert Graysmith
mentioned in the paper today?

2024
02:02:33.741 --> 02:02:36.835
- Yeah?
- I can tell you who the Zodiac is.

2025
02:02:40.648 --> 02:02:41.672
Who is this?

2026
02:02:41.782 --> 02:02:43.909
The Zodiac Killer
is obsessed with movies.

2027
02:02:44.018 --> 02:02:46.714
He recorded his murders on film.

2028
02:02:46.821 --> 02:02:50.188
I tried to tell the police,
but they wouldn't follow through on it.

2029
02:02:50.291 --> 02:02:53.226
There's a man you need to find.
His name is Bob Vaughn.

2030
02:02:53.327 --> 02:02:55.852
- Pen, pen.
- V-A-U-G-H-N.

2031
02:02:55.963 --> 02:02:58.090
He's a friend of the Zodiac's.

2032
02:02:58.199 --> 02:03:00.326
Mr. Vaughn does not know
his friend is a killer,

2033
02:03:00.434 --> 02:03:03.028
and he is storing
some film canisters for him.

2034
02:03:03.137 --> 02:03:04.832
In these canisters is the evidence.

2035
02:03:04.939 --> 02:03:08.306
Okay, yeah, friend? Who is this friend?

2036
02:03:08.409 --> 02:03:10.036
You have quite enough to get started.

2037
02:03:10.144 --> 02:03:11.873
Oh, please.

2038
02:03:11.979 --> 02:03:15.278
The Zodiac's name is Rick Marshall.

2039
02:03:19.153 --> 02:03:20.984
Your toast is burning.

2040
02:03:22.023 --> 02:03:27.015
We choose at some point in our lives
how to physically construct each letter.

2041
02:03:27.828 --> 02:03:30.023
Once we lock that into our brains,

2042
02:03:30.131 --> 02:03:32.429
our handwriting may change
over the years,

2043
02:03:32.533 --> 02:03:35.195
but the moves themselves
remain unaltered.

2044
02:03:35.302 --> 02:03:36.792
- Understand?
- Yes.

2045
02:03:38.406 --> 02:03:40.340
Except Zodiac's doesn't.

2046
02:03:41.942 --> 02:03:43.876
Specifically with his "K."

2047
02:03:45.112 --> 02:03:48.013
In his first letters,
he executed the "K" with two strokes.

2048
02:03:48.115 --> 02:03:49.582
Later letters, he did them with three.

2049
02:03:49.683 --> 02:03:51.947
- Why?
- We don't know.

2050
02:03:52.053 --> 02:03:53.987
Excuse me, I've got to spray this.

2051
02:03:54.088 --> 02:03:57.216
How many suspects
were cleared through handwriting?

2052
02:03:57.324 --> 02:03:58.757
All of them.

2053
02:03:58.859 --> 02:04:02.317
Also the print in the cab.
No match was ever found.

2054
02:04:02.430 --> 02:04:06.457
Is there any way that someone
could beat a handwriting test?

2055
02:04:06.567 --> 02:04:07.556
No.

2056
02:04:07.668 --> 02:04:10.831
Whoever the Zodiac is,
he's not someone I cleared.

2057
02:04:11.772 --> 02:04:15.230
About a month ago, a man showed up
on my doorstep very distraught.

2058
02:04:15.342 --> 02:04:17.401
His name was Wallace Penny.

2059
02:04:18.345 --> 02:04:20.609
He said he knew who the Zodiac was.

2060
02:04:20.714 --> 02:04:22.739
Gave me a name.

2061
02:04:22.850 --> 02:04:25.045
Rick. Rick somebody.

2062
02:04:25.152 --> 02:04:27.552
- Rick Marshall?
- Yeah.

2063
02:04:27.655 --> 02:04:30.180
I think that the man
who you talked to called me, too.

2064
02:04:30.291 --> 02:04:32.885
After he left, then I checked my files.

2065
02:04:32.993 --> 02:04:34.688
I never cleared a Rick Marshall.

2066
02:04:41.969 --> 02:04:43.095
Hello?

2067
02:04:48.275 --> 02:04:49.970
Hello? Who is this?

2068
02:05:00.154 --> 02:05:02.054
It's a wrong number.

2069
02:05:08.028 --> 02:05:11.156
Does the name Rick Marshall
mean anything to you?

2070
02:05:12.199 --> 02:05:14.224
What are you after?

2071
02:05:14.335 --> 02:05:15.393
What do you got?

2072
02:05:15.503 --> 02:05:19.735
Hypothetically, you just named
my favorite suspect in the whole case.

2073
02:05:20.908 --> 02:05:22.375
This is off the record.

2074
02:05:22.476 --> 02:05:24.808
Couple years back,
I was trying to get Marshall's prints.

2075
02:05:24.912 --> 02:05:26.641
I handed him a photo.

2076
02:05:26.747 --> 02:05:29.113
He looks at it. He's about to give it back
and he stops and he says,

2077
02:05:29.216 --> 02:05:31.650
"My goodness,
I got fingerprints all over this."

2078
02:05:31.752 --> 02:05:33.583
And he wipes them off.

2079
02:05:34.321 --> 02:05:36.016
Why didn't you test him for handwriting?

2080
02:05:36.123 --> 02:05:38.751
Because when they finally
did run his prints,

2081
02:05:38.859 --> 02:05:41.123
they cleared him
against the one in Stine's cab.

2082
02:05:41.228 --> 02:05:43.321
- So, then, it's not him.
- Maybe yes, maybe no.

2083
02:05:43.430 --> 02:05:45.455
No. What do you mean?

2084
02:05:45.566 --> 02:05:47.932
Zodiac left gloves behind at the scene.

2085
02:05:48.035 --> 02:05:50.060
If he had the foresight
to bring gloves with him,

2086
02:05:50.171 --> 02:05:52.162
how the hell's he gonna
accidentally leave a print behind?

2087
02:05:52.273 --> 02:05:54.264
But it was in the victim's blood.

2088
02:05:54.375 --> 02:05:55.706
Could have been one of the bystanders,

2089
02:05:55.809 --> 02:05:58.175
or a cop just reaches out,
boom, false print.

2090
02:05:58.279 --> 02:06:00.645
Yeah, but that print
disqualified 2,500 suspects.

2091
02:06:00.748 --> 02:06:02.045
Which is why we also used handwriting.

2092
02:06:02.149 --> 02:06:03.446
But not for Rick Marshall.

2093
02:06:03.551 --> 02:06:06.611
SFPD saw a handwritten sign
in the window of his house.

2094
02:06:06.720 --> 02:06:10.554
Decided it looked nothing
like the Z letters, so they just moved on.

2095
02:06:10.658 --> 02:06:12.888
How do they know
that Rick Marshall wrote the sign?

2096
02:06:12.993 --> 02:06:14.255
My thoughts exactly.

2097
02:06:15.262 --> 02:06:18.925
Rick Marshall was a Navy man.
He received code training.

2098
02:06:19.033 --> 02:06:21.467
He was also a projectionist
at a silent film theater.

2099
02:06:21.569 --> 02:06:23.662
Well, then, how do I get copies
of Rick Marshall's handwriting?

2100
02:06:23.771 --> 02:06:27.639
Three ways.
One, get a warrant, which you can't.

2101
02:06:27.741 --> 02:06:29.868
Two, get him to volunteer,
which he won't.

2102
02:06:29.977 --> 02:06:31.877
Yeah, and three?

2103
02:06:31.979 --> 02:06:33.606
Get creative.

2104
02:06:33.714 --> 02:06:36.444
I don't know what to tell you.
You get it, I'll analyze it.

2105
02:06:36.550 --> 02:06:37.915
Beyond that, you're on your own.

2106
02:06:38.018 --> 02:06:40.452
Okay, what about
the guy who came to see you,

2107
02:06:40.554 --> 02:06:41.953
the one who called me?

2108
02:06:42.056 --> 02:06:44.524
You mean Wallace Penny?

2109
02:06:44.625 --> 02:06:46.718
Yeah. Did he leave a number?

2110
02:06:56.070 --> 02:06:59.335
- Hello?
- Hi, this is Robert Graysmith.

2111
02:06:59.440 --> 02:07:00.429
How did you find me?

2112
02:07:00.541 --> 02:07:02.566
I need a sample
of Rick Marshall's handwriting.

2113
02:07:02.676 --> 02:07:03.973
I told you. Vaughn is who...

2114
02:07:04.078 --> 02:07:07.047
Mr. Penny,
if Rick Marshall is the Zodiac,

2115
02:07:07.147 --> 02:07:09.615
I need a sample of his handwriting
to confirm it.

2116
02:07:09.717 --> 02:07:11.309
Can you help me or not?

2117
02:07:13.020 --> 02:07:17.684
Rick used to draw movie posters
for the theater Vaughn worked at.

2118
02:07:17.791 --> 02:07:19.691
- I'll send one down.
- Thank you.

2119
02:07:29.703 --> 02:07:32.103
- I'll need to see more samples.
- Yeah, but is it...

2120
02:07:32.206 --> 02:07:34.697
It's as close as I've ever seen.
We have to tread lightly here.

2121
02:07:34.808 --> 02:07:37.242
We're talking about
implicating this man as the Zodiac.

2122
02:07:37.344 --> 02:07:40.336
I can get more. I'll just find Vaughn
and I'll track down Linda.

2123
02:07:40.447 --> 02:07:42.415
I mean, Linda is Darlene's sister.

2124
02:07:42.516 --> 02:07:45.212
I've been to the DMV,
and I talked to her parents,

2125
02:07:45.319 --> 02:07:48.413
but still, nobody knows
where to find her.

2126
02:07:48.522 --> 02:07:52.982
Mr. Graysmith, most of the writing
matches the exemplar.

2127
02:07:53.093 --> 02:07:56.119
In a way, though, it's the part that
doesn't match that scares me the most.

2128
02:07:56.230 --> 02:07:58.630
- What do you mean?
- Well, on the poster,

2129
02:07:58.732 --> 02:08:01.826
the one letter that absolutely,
positively does not match

2130
02:08:01.935 --> 02:08:03.493
is the letter "K."

2131
02:08:05.506 --> 02:08:09.374
You wouldn't happen to have any
animal crackers in there, would you?

2132
02:08:09.476 --> 02:08:13.037
Unit Five.
Toschi needs to call in on a landline.

2133
02:08:25.059 --> 02:08:27.425
- Dispatch.
- Hey. Dave Toschi.

2134
02:08:27.528 --> 02:08:29.120
I'll connect you.

2135
02:08:30.064 --> 02:08:31.463
- Dave?
- Yeah. What's up?

2136
02:08:31.565 --> 02:08:33.999
Jennings here from the Chronicle.

2137
02:08:34.101 --> 02:08:35.898
It came in this morning
and you need to see it right now.

2138
02:08:36.003 --> 02:08:37.061
See what?

2139
02:08:37.171 --> 02:08:39.901
The new Zodiac letter.
And it mentions you.

2140
02:08:40.007 --> 02:08:41.065
Okay, okay.

2141
02:08:43.377 --> 02:08:45.641
Shit. All right, come on.

2142
02:08:45.746 --> 02:08:47.680
Hall of Justice!

2143
02:08:47.781 --> 02:08:50.841
Now! Come on, come on,
come on, come on, come on!

2144
02:08:57.191 --> 02:08:58.249
Dave!

2145
02:08:59.393 --> 02:09:01.327
Do you have it with you?

2146
02:09:04.598 --> 02:09:06.793
"This is the Zodiac speaking.
I'm back with you.

2147
02:09:06.900 --> 02:09:09.960
"Tell Herb Caen I am here,
I have always been here.

2148
02:09:10.070 --> 02:09:13.096
"That city pig Toschi is good,
but I am smarter and better.

2149
02:09:13.207 --> 02:09:16.074
"He will get tired, then leave me alone.

2150
02:09:16.176 --> 02:09:19.475
"I'm waiting for a good movie about me.
Who will play me?

2151
02:09:19.580 --> 02:09:21.673
"I'm now in control of all things."

2152
02:09:21.782 --> 02:09:24.444
These guys are from Internal Affairs.

2153
02:09:26.286 --> 02:09:27.878
We need to talk.

2154
02:09:27.988 --> 02:09:29.746
Good evening. Our top story tonight,

2155
02:09:29.857 --> 02:09:32.348
the San Francisco Police Department
has confirmed

2156
02:09:32.459 --> 02:09:34.950
that the man
who calls himself the Zodiac

2157
02:09:35.062 --> 02:09:39.431
and terrorized the Bay Area
has broken his silence of 51 months.

2158
02:09:39.533 --> 02:09:42.161
In a letter claiming,
"I am back with you,"

2159
02:09:42.269 --> 02:09:45.898
the Zodiac makes no overt threats
against the citizenry,

2160
02:09:46.006 --> 02:09:48.839
and muses that his life and times
would make the best movie script yet.

2161
02:09:48.942 --> 02:09:50.432
These carrots are perfect.

2162
02:09:50.544 --> 02:09:51.909
The terse 66 word message
also manages...

2163
02:09:52.012 --> 02:09:53.036
Just go.

2164
02:09:53.147 --> 02:09:56.116
...to mention San Francisco Chronicle
columnist Herb Caen

2165
02:09:56.216 --> 02:09:59.151
and the Department's own
David Toschi by name.

2166
02:09:59.253 --> 02:10:00.845
- May I be excused?
- Are they targets?

2167
02:10:00.954 --> 02:10:01.943
Fine, but you have to come back

2168
02:10:02.055 --> 02:10:03.682
and finish at least half
of what's on that plate.

2169
02:10:03.791 --> 02:10:04.883
More team coverage
on the cipher slayer's return...

2170
02:10:04.992 --> 02:10:05.981
- Okay?
- Okay.

2171
02:10:06.093 --> 02:10:08.561
...begins as Alan Freeman has more.

2172
02:10:08.662 --> 02:10:09.788
Thank you, Eric.

2173
02:10:09.897 --> 02:10:12.365
San Francisco Chronicle columnist
Armistead Maupin says

2174
02:10:12.466 --> 02:10:15.060
that he thinks not only
is this new letter a forgery,

2175
02:10:15.169 --> 02:10:17.103
but it was written by the very man

2176
02:10:17.204 --> 02:10:20.935
trusted to hunt down this killer,
David Toschi.

2177
02:10:21.041 --> 02:10:24.704
Maupin, a very well-respected author,
has gone on record saying

2178
02:10:24.812 --> 02:10:29.408
that he believes Toschi wrote the letter
to drum up publicity for himself.

2179
02:10:29.516 --> 02:10:32.576
Maupin used David
as a character in his column.

2180
02:10:32.686 --> 02:10:34.586
David got a kick out of it

2181
02:10:34.688 --> 02:10:36.679
and so he wrote
a couple of anonymous letters

2182
02:10:36.790 --> 02:10:38.690
asking for the character
to be brought back.

2183
02:10:38.792 --> 02:10:41.784
It was like
writing fan mail to himself. That's all.

2184
02:10:41.895 --> 02:10:44.090
But David did not write that letter.

2185
02:10:44.198 --> 02:10:47.326
No, I'm sure that he didn't.
And I'm sure that this will all blow over.

2186
02:10:47.434 --> 02:10:48.765
Blow over?

2187
02:10:48.869 --> 02:10:51.064
They kicked him out of Homicide.

2188
02:10:51.171 --> 02:10:54.436
They made him give his handwriting
like some common criminal.

2189
02:10:54.541 --> 02:10:56.873
- May I talk to him?
- No.

2190
02:10:57.945 --> 02:10:59.105
Okay, can you just ask him

2191
02:10:59.213 --> 02:11:01.579
if he ever investigated
a man named Rick Marshall?

2192
02:11:01.682 --> 02:11:03.445
Is that all you can think about?

2193
02:11:03.550 --> 02:11:06.951
Mr. Graysmith,
Maupin works at your paper. We trust...

2194
02:11:12.759 --> 02:11:14.124
This girl, she wants music lessons?

2195
02:11:14.228 --> 02:11:15.695
Dave! Dave!

2196
02:11:18.198 --> 02:11:20.393
I'll catch up to you.

2197
02:11:20.501 --> 02:11:22.696
You stop calling my house.
Do you understand me?

2198
02:11:22.803 --> 02:11:24.498
I just need your help to find Linda.

2199
02:11:24.605 --> 02:11:26.664
- Jesus.
- Look, two seconds.

2200
02:11:28.642 --> 02:11:31.042
Look, we've been
running handwriting samples.

2201
02:11:31.144 --> 02:11:33.374
- Who's we?
- Sherwood and I.

2202
02:11:33.480 --> 02:11:34.572
Sherwood?

2203
02:11:34.681 --> 02:11:36.774
Sherwood who was fired
from Questioned Documents?

2204
02:11:36.884 --> 02:11:38.442
Sherwood who drinks
like Paul Avery now?

2205
02:11:38.552 --> 02:11:41.043
- He retired.
- Is that what he told you?

2206
02:11:41.154 --> 02:11:45.318
- What, are you saying he's wrong?
- I'm saying stop calling my house.

2207
02:11:45.926 --> 02:11:47.450
- We ran them on Rick Marshall.
- No, Robert.

2208
02:11:47.561 --> 02:11:48.858
No, I know you don't think it's him.

2209
02:11:48.962 --> 02:11:50.395
I mean, no, I am not having
this conversation.

2210
02:11:50.497 --> 02:11:53.330
But I think that Marshall knew Darlene,
and I can't talk to Mageau or Linda,

2211
02:11:53.433 --> 02:11:54.422
so I'm gonna talk to Bob Vaughn.

2212
02:11:54.535 --> 02:11:55.763
- Robert. Robert, stop it!
- What?

2213
02:11:55.869 --> 02:11:58.099
Okay, the Rick Marshalls
of this world will suck you dry.

2214
02:11:58.205 --> 02:11:59.172
They're blind alleys.

2215
02:11:59.273 --> 02:12:01.741
But he said he wasn't gonna announce
his murders anymore, Dave.

2216
02:12:01.842 --> 02:12:02.900
He was just gonna do them.

2217
02:12:03.010 --> 02:12:05.945
Do you know what the chances
of us arresting someone are now?

2218
02:12:06.046 --> 02:12:10.142
Too much time has gone by, okay?
Too much of the evidence is lost.

2219
02:12:10.250 --> 02:12:13.413
People get old, Robert. They forget.

2220
02:12:13.520 --> 02:12:17.650
Now, I have been a cop for 25 years.
Murder police for 12.

2221
02:12:17.758 --> 02:12:20.056
- What do you do for a living?
- You know what I do for a living.

2222
02:12:20.160 --> 02:12:22.390
- You're a cartoonist.
- So what are you saying?

2223
02:12:22.496 --> 02:12:25.624
I am saying Zodiac was my job.
It is not yours.

2224
02:12:28.869 --> 02:12:31.201
- He's still out there, Dave.
- No, Robert. I am through with this.

2225
02:12:31.305 --> 02:12:33.170
I am through with you.

2226
02:12:39.546 --> 02:12:42.037
What about September 26, 1970?

2227
02:12:42.149 --> 02:12:45.676
- Okay, which one was that?
- The Lake Tahoe nurse goes missing.

2228
02:12:48.689 --> 02:12:50.020
One day before the vernal equinox.

2229
02:12:50.123 --> 02:12:52.023
- Dad?
- Yeah. Mark that.

2230
02:12:52.125 --> 02:12:55.754
Got another one. June 19th, 1971.

2231
02:12:55.862 --> 02:12:58.626
That's got to be
near the summer solstice.

2232
02:13:01.001 --> 02:13:02.263
Oh, guys.

2233
02:13:02.369 --> 02:13:05.395
Don't tell Mom about
our special project, okay?

2234
02:13:05.939 --> 02:13:09.534
How come you and Mom
don't sleep in the same bed anymore?

2235
02:13:13.113 --> 02:13:14.080
Hello.

2236
02:13:14.181 --> 02:13:16.240
Mr. Graysmith,
it's Ken Narlow from Napa.

2237
02:13:16.350 --> 02:13:20.616
Oh, Captain Narlow.
Thank you for calling me back.

2238
02:13:20.721 --> 02:13:22.586
Yeah. How can I help?

2239
02:13:22.689 --> 02:13:25.351
I called you because we've been
cross-referencing lunar cycles

2240
02:13:25.459 --> 02:13:27.120
with the Zodiac's timeline.

2241
02:13:27.227 --> 02:13:31.459
More often than not, each cycle
since '69 corresponds with an attack

2242
02:13:31.565 --> 02:13:34.432
or with one of the letters,
or an unsolved homicide.

2243
02:13:34.534 --> 02:13:37.367
- Who's working with you on this?
- Some colleagues.

2244
02:13:37.471 --> 02:13:38.495
Dad?

2245
02:13:39.840 --> 02:13:42.274
- Ken, can you hold on one second?
- Dad?

2246
02:13:42.376 --> 02:13:44.367
- What is it?
- What's this?

2247
02:13:48.248 --> 02:13:51.308
In the decade since the Zodiac's
last cipher was received,

2248
02:13:51.418 --> 02:13:54.876
every federal agency
has taken a crack at decoding it.

2249
02:13:54.988 --> 02:13:57.752
But today,
where those agencies had failed,

2250
02:13:57.858 --> 02:14:00.486
a cartoonist has succeeded.

2251
02:14:00.594 --> 02:14:02.118
How did you do it?

2252
02:14:02.229 --> 02:14:07.633
Oh, just a lot of books from the library,
and I love puzzles, so I just...

2253
02:14:09.736 --> 02:14:11.931
Yeah. The fucking library.

2254
02:14:12.039 --> 02:14:15.167
I believe that you can accomplish
anything that you put your mind...

2255
02:14:18.078 --> 02:14:20.842
That's a "J"? Okay. Honor Camp?

2256
02:14:22.482 --> 02:14:24.109
Thank you so much.

2257
02:14:26.119 --> 02:14:28.349
Hey, we found Linda.
She's in jail. Isn't that great?

2258
02:14:28.455 --> 02:14:29.581
Why'd you do it?

2259
02:14:29.690 --> 02:14:31.123
Because she'll be able to identify Rick...

2260
02:14:31.224 --> 02:14:33.920
- What are you talking about?
- You went on TV.

2261
02:14:34.528 --> 02:14:36.189
You put yourself out there
for him to see.

2262
02:14:36.296 --> 02:14:37.786
Oh, hon, you're being paranoid.

2263
02:14:37.898 --> 02:14:39.889
Then who's been calling our house
in the middle of the night

2264
02:14:40.000 --> 02:14:40.989
at least once a week?

2265
02:14:41.101 --> 02:14:42.261
Nobody.

2266
02:14:44.271 --> 02:14:45.932
What's it gonna take
for you to be done with this?

2267
02:14:46.039 --> 02:14:48.940
I can't talk about this now.
I have to go see Bob Vaughn.

2268
02:14:49.042 --> 02:14:52.375
Well, that's too bad,
because we're gonna talk about this.

2269
02:14:52.479 --> 02:14:54.811
And when is it gonna be finished?

2270
02:14:54.915 --> 02:14:56.746
When you catch him?
When you arrest him?

2271
02:14:56.850 --> 02:14:59.045
- Be serious.
- I am serious.

2272
02:15:00.887 --> 02:15:04.379
I need to know who he is.

2273
02:15:04.491 --> 02:15:07.619
I need to stand there,

2274
02:15:07.728 --> 02:15:11.630
I need to look him in the eye
and I need to know that it's him.

2275
02:15:13.533 --> 02:15:15.797
Is that more important
than your family's safety?

2276
02:15:15.902 --> 02:15:17.369
Of course not.

2277
02:15:19.372 --> 02:15:21.738
Why? Why do you need to do this?

2278
02:15:23.643 --> 02:15:24.701
Why?

2279
02:15:26.713 --> 02:15:28.681
Because nobody else will.

2280
02:15:28.782 --> 02:15:30.716
That's not good enough.

2281
02:15:30.817 --> 02:15:32.682
Are you done? Can I go?

2282
02:15:48.001 --> 02:15:50.026
- Mr. Vaughn?
- Mr. Graysmith?

2283
02:15:50.137 --> 02:15:51.161
- Yes.
- Hi.

2284
02:15:51.271 --> 02:15:52.602
You needed to speak to me?

2285
02:15:52.706 --> 02:15:55.106
Yes. There's a coffee shop
right on the corner.

2286
02:15:55.208 --> 02:15:58.268
- Why don't we just go to my home?
- Oh, I don't wanna put you out.

2287
02:15:58.378 --> 02:16:00.278
It's no trouble at all.

2288
02:16:00.380 --> 02:16:02.848
- Where are you parked?
- Just right there.

2289
02:16:02.949 --> 02:16:06.282
- You can follow me.
- Oh. Okay.

2290
02:16:25.005 --> 02:16:26.563
Watch your step.

2291
02:16:28.074 --> 02:16:29.735
Come in.

2292
02:16:31.178 --> 02:16:34.306
- Very nice house.
- Oh, thank you.

2293
02:16:34.414 --> 02:16:36.245
It's very rustic.

2294
02:16:36.349 --> 02:16:39.512
- Can I take your jacket?
- No, thank you, I'm fine.

2295
02:16:39.619 --> 02:16:41.587
Okay. This way, please.

2296
02:16:44.391 --> 02:16:46.120
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

2297
02:16:46.226 --> 02:16:48.751
- How about some tea?
- Oh, no, I'm all right.

2298
02:16:48.862 --> 02:16:50.295
- You sure?
- Yes.

2299
02:16:51.198 --> 02:16:54.929
I wanted to ask you about a film
that the Avenue may have played

2300
02:16:55.035 --> 02:16:56.935
while you were the organist there.

2301
02:16:57.037 --> 02:16:59.301
The Most Dangerous Game?

2302
02:16:59.406 --> 02:17:02.739
Oh, it's a classic. RKO. 1932.

2303
02:17:02.843 --> 02:17:07.542
Fay Wray, Joel McCrea, Leslie Banks.
We've run that picture many times.

2304
02:17:07.647 --> 02:17:09.137
In '68, '69?

2305
02:17:10.784 --> 02:17:12.979
I'd have to check my records. Why?

2306
02:17:13.086 --> 02:17:15.145
Do you remember the Zodiac?

2307
02:17:17.390 --> 02:17:19.654
This is about Rick Marshall, isn't it?

2308
02:17:19.759 --> 02:17:23.160
- He was a projectionist there, right?
- For a time, yes.

2309
02:17:23.263 --> 02:17:27.290
But I have no occasion
to correspond with him these days.

2310
02:17:27.400 --> 02:17:29.868
Okay. Well, there is a connection

2311
02:17:29.970 --> 02:17:32.734
between one of the Zodiac attacks
and that film.

2312
02:17:32.839 --> 02:17:34.568
You mean the symbol?

2313
02:17:35.842 --> 02:17:37.036
Hold on.

2314
02:17:37.611 --> 02:17:41.707
The Zodiac symbol on film.
It's on the countdown.

2315
02:17:45.619 --> 02:17:48.213
It's trimmed off each reel
before it's shown,

2316
02:17:48.321 --> 02:17:50.846
but it always arrives with it.

2317
02:17:50.957 --> 02:17:52.322
Right there.

2318
02:17:52.959 --> 02:17:56.622
The first time I saw it in the papers,
I thought about that.

2319
02:17:57.497 --> 02:17:59.021
We got a tip

2320
02:17:59.132 --> 02:18:03.091
that Rick left a film canister here
that he told you never to open.

2321
02:18:03.203 --> 02:18:06.331
A tip about a mysterious film canister?

2322
02:18:07.207 --> 02:18:08.538
Is it true?

2323
02:18:10.477 --> 02:18:11.637
Yes.

2324
02:18:12.345 --> 02:18:14.643
- Did you open it?
- No.

2325
02:18:14.748 --> 02:18:19.014
- May I see it?
- Rick took it back in 1972.

2326
02:18:20.754 --> 02:18:25.521
This tip is how you got it in your head
that Rick is the Zodiac?

2327
02:18:25.625 --> 02:18:27.286
That and the poster.

2328
02:18:27.394 --> 02:18:28.725
The poster?

2329
02:18:30.697 --> 02:18:32.460
The poster that Rick drew.

2330
02:18:32.565 --> 02:18:35.762
The handwriting is the closest
that we have ever come to a match.

2331
02:18:35.869 --> 02:18:39.134
- Rick didn't draw any posters.
- No, he drew this one.

2332
02:18:39.239 --> 02:18:42.675
Mr. Graysmith, I do the posters myself.

2333
02:18:44.077 --> 02:18:45.908
That's my handwriting.

2334
02:18:54.187 --> 02:18:57.054
I won't take any more of your time.

2335
02:18:57.157 --> 02:19:02.527
Why don't I just go and find out
when we played that film?

2336
02:19:02.629 --> 02:19:04.096
Oh, that's all right.

2337
02:19:04.197 --> 02:19:07.598
It's not a problem.
They're just down in the basement.

2338
02:19:09.436 --> 02:19:12.337
Not many people
have basements in California.

2339
02:19:15.041 --> 02:19:16.099
I do.

2340
02:19:18.311 --> 02:19:20.279
You coming, Mr. Graysmith?

2341
02:19:31.591 --> 02:19:35.254
The original studio one-sheets,
I always kept for myself.

2342
02:19:37.163 --> 02:19:39.688
The cheapo knock-offs
like you brought today

2343
02:19:39.799 --> 02:19:42.927
I end up tossing into the back alley.

2344
02:19:57.450 --> 02:19:58.940
'69.

2345
02:20:04.657 --> 02:20:05.885
You live alone?

2346
02:20:05.992 --> 02:20:11.760
Most Dangerous Game ran in May '69.

2347
02:20:11.865 --> 02:20:14.299
So, that would be about

2348
02:20:15.235 --> 02:20:18.500
nine weeks before
the first Zodiac letter, correct?

2349
02:20:21.441 --> 02:20:22.499
Yeah.

2350
02:20:27.013 --> 02:20:31.279
Do you think he saw the film
in our theater and was inspired?

2351
02:20:37.390 --> 02:20:40.257
Are you sure
there's nobody else in the house?

2352
02:20:41.895 --> 02:20:44.557
Would you like
to go upstairs and check?

2353
02:20:45.298 --> 02:20:46.287
No.

2354
02:20:49.436 --> 02:20:51.961
Thank you. Thanks for everything.

2355
02:20:52.839 --> 02:20:54.306
You're welcome.

2356
02:21:15.628 --> 02:21:16.993
It's locked.

2357
02:21:27.874 --> 02:21:29.171
Thank you.

2358
02:21:32.312 --> 02:21:34.303
Good night, Mr. Graysmith!

2359
02:21:54.267 --> 02:21:57.930
Two killers. Got to be two killers.
One has the...

2360
02:22:05.812 --> 02:22:06.972
Guys?

2361
02:22:40.547 --> 02:22:42.481
You've got five minutes.

2362
02:22:50.657 --> 02:22:51.783
Linda?

2363
02:22:52.959 --> 02:22:54.426
Hi, I'm Robert.

2364
02:22:58.398 --> 02:23:00.127
Did you get my note?

2365
02:23:01.100 --> 02:23:03.068
- What's this about?
- Zodiac.

2366
02:23:04.637 --> 02:23:05.831
Figures.

2367
02:23:07.207 --> 02:23:09.937
- You got the look.
- What look?

2368
02:23:10.043 --> 02:23:12.034
I didn't mean anything.

2369
02:23:13.279 --> 02:23:15.645
Tell me about this painting party.

2370
02:23:16.849 --> 02:23:19.443
I told the cops about that so long ago.

2371
02:23:22.922 --> 02:23:24.685
Darlene always had
a lot of boys around,

2372
02:23:24.791 --> 02:23:26.725
even though she was married.

2373
02:23:26.826 --> 02:23:28.817
And this one guy was weird, though.

2374
02:23:28.928 --> 02:23:32.261
He used to bring her presents
from Tijuana and...

2375
02:23:33.499 --> 02:23:36.093
I don't know why
she was friends with him.

2376
02:23:36.202 --> 02:23:38.670
She once told me he'd killed somebody.

2377
02:23:38.771 --> 02:23:40.329
Really?

2378
02:23:40.440 --> 02:23:42.635
Yeah, I think maybe
when he was in the service.

2379
02:23:42.742 --> 02:23:44.710
- Navy?
- I think so.

2380
02:23:44.811 --> 02:23:46.972
Was he into movies?
Was he a movie buff?

2381
02:23:47.080 --> 02:23:49.981
I can tell you that
he was not into people.

2382
02:23:50.083 --> 02:23:51.414
The party Darlene threw,

2383
02:23:51.517 --> 02:23:54.418
people were supposed to
just show up and drink beer, help paint.

2384
02:23:54.520 --> 02:23:56.750
But this guy showed up in a suit,

2385
02:23:56.856 --> 02:23:59.791
and just sat in a chair
all by himself all night long.

2386
02:23:59.892 --> 02:24:01.325
Didn't talk to anyone.

2387
02:24:01.427 --> 02:24:03.258
And Darlene told me
to stay away from him.

2388
02:24:03.363 --> 02:24:05.194
She was scared of him.

2389
02:24:07.467 --> 02:24:09.935
And a couple of weeks later,
she was dead.

2390
02:24:10.036 --> 02:24:12.504
I'm sorry. Do you remember his name?

2391
02:24:13.506 --> 02:24:17.374
I mean, it was short,
like a nickname, like Stan.

2392
02:24:17.477 --> 02:24:19.775
- Rick?
- No, I don't think so.

2393
02:24:20.680 --> 02:24:22.875
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

2394
02:24:22.982 --> 02:24:25.507
How can you be sure?
It was a long time ago. Think hard.

2395
02:24:25.618 --> 02:24:27.643
I am thinking hard.

2396
02:24:27.754 --> 02:24:29.119
It was Rick.

2397
02:24:30.156 --> 02:24:31.248
No, it wasn't.

2398
02:24:31.357 --> 02:24:33.723
- It was Rick. It was Rick Marshall.
- No.

2399
02:24:33.826 --> 02:24:35.521
Just say it!

2400
02:24:35.628 --> 02:24:37.459
It wasn't Rick.

2401
02:24:50.243 --> 02:24:51.574
It was Leigh.

2402
02:24:54.747 --> 02:24:57.275
- Leigh?
- Yeah, Leigh.

2403
02:24:58.618 --> 02:24:59.915
Sounds right.

2404
02:25:04.757 --> 02:25:07.590
Officer! I need you to let me in.

2405
02:25:07.694 --> 02:25:09.821
- Is this an emergency?
- No, I just need to see one file.

2406
02:25:09.929 --> 02:25:11.556
No, you need to come back
tomorrow morning.

2407
02:25:11.664 --> 02:25:13.859
- One file, just for one second.
- 8:00 a.m., when we're open.

2408
02:25:13.966 --> 02:25:15.593
Sergeant! Sergeant Mulanax!

2409
02:25:15.702 --> 02:25:18.136
Sergeant, I just need to see one file!

2410
02:25:18.237 --> 02:25:21.638
Just give me five minutes.
I know exactly where it is.

2411
02:25:22.642 --> 02:25:23.802
Please!

2412
02:25:37.190 --> 02:25:38.851
I shouldn't be talking to you.

2413
02:25:38.958 --> 02:25:40.949
- You got five minutes.
- Okay.

2414
02:25:43.229 --> 02:25:44.457
Here. Here.

2415
02:25:44.564 --> 02:25:48.330
Linda states that some of
Darlene's closest friends are Leigh,

2416
02:25:48.434 --> 02:25:51.403
who used to bring Darlene
presents from Tijuana.

2417
02:25:51.504 --> 02:25:53.404
- So what?
- He knew her.

2418
02:25:53.506 --> 02:25:55.201
Linda said Leigh. This is Leigh.

2419
02:25:55.308 --> 02:25:57.742
No. That's just one name in a file
that contains hundreds.

2420
02:25:57.844 --> 02:25:59.277
It's nothing.

2421
02:26:00.046 --> 02:26:02.207
- Dave Toschi...
- Agrees with me.

2422
02:26:02.749 --> 02:26:05.616
Our investigation
into this subject is over.

2423
02:26:08.621 --> 02:26:09.883
I'm sorry.

2424
02:26:19.065 --> 02:26:20.191
Hello.

2425
02:26:35.381 --> 02:26:36.780
Who's there?

2426
02:26:40.253 --> 02:26:43.745
- You didn't return my calls.
- Oh, I've been kind of busy.

2427
02:26:43.856 --> 02:26:45.687
Yeah. I can see that.

2428
02:26:47.927 --> 02:26:49.758
How's the book coming?

2429
02:26:52.832 --> 02:26:54.823
I tried to send you these.

2430
02:26:55.935 --> 02:26:57.698
I called the Chron.

2431
02:26:57.804 --> 02:27:00.568
Well, I'm not a cartoonist anymore, so...

2432
02:27:02.141 --> 02:27:03.335
I heard.

2433
02:27:08.514 --> 02:27:11.108
When's the last time
you ate something?

2434
02:27:13.653 --> 02:27:15.746
Nothing makes sense anymore.

2435
02:27:18.458 --> 02:27:20.722
- Did it ever?
- Yeah, it did.

2436
02:27:22.228 --> 02:27:25.129
Robert, it was just the date
that didn't end.

2437
02:27:25.631 --> 02:27:27.394
You don't mean that.

2438
02:27:28.835 --> 02:27:30.029
A little.

2439
02:27:32.905 --> 02:27:34.702
The kids miss you.

2440
02:27:34.807 --> 02:27:37.901
- I can't have them see me like this.
- Neither can I.

2441
02:27:38.678 --> 02:27:40.771
So, do whatever you have to,

2442
02:27:41.747 --> 02:27:43.271
but finish this.

2443
02:28:10.843 --> 02:28:11.901
Dave!

2444
02:28:12.778 --> 02:28:14.405
Dave! It's Robert!

2445
02:28:16.582 --> 02:28:18.209
- Dave!
- Is he actually here?

2446
02:28:18.317 --> 02:28:20.012
I'm gonna kill him.

2447
02:28:20.386 --> 02:28:22.980
I'm calling SFPD. Where's my gun?

2448
02:28:25.558 --> 02:28:26.684
Dave!

2449
02:28:26.792 --> 02:28:28.521
Robert! Go away!

2450
02:28:28.628 --> 02:28:30.596
Dave! He made a mistake!

2451
02:28:30.696 --> 02:28:32.664
- Get away from the window.
- I'll meet you around front.

2452
02:28:32.765 --> 02:28:34.232
No, you won't.

2453
02:28:35.401 --> 02:28:37.596
- You have to hear this!
- No, I don't, Robert!

2454
02:28:37.703 --> 02:28:40.171
The birthday was the one time
that he was weak!

2455
02:28:40.273 --> 02:28:42.070
The one time
that he gave something away!

2456
02:28:42.174 --> 02:28:45.473
- Robert, I am calling the police.
- It's Arthur Leigh Allen!

2457
02:28:50.516 --> 02:28:52.780
Where did you get that name?

2458
02:28:52.885 --> 02:28:54.409
He called the Bellis' house.

2459
02:28:54.520 --> 02:28:56.750
December '69.
"I need to kill. Today's my birthday."

2460
02:28:56.856 --> 02:28:58.824
It was his birthday.

2461
02:28:58.925 --> 02:29:01.826
Arthur Leigh Allen
was born on December 18th.

2462
02:29:04.897 --> 02:29:06.262
Get in here.

2463
02:29:08.401 --> 02:29:10.562
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

2464
02:29:13.539 --> 02:29:15.370
He wrote me, you know?

2465
02:29:16.075 --> 02:29:17.201
2,500 suspects,

2466
02:29:17.310 --> 02:29:20.871
the only one who ever wrote me
a letter was Leigh Allen.

2467
02:29:21.814 --> 02:29:23.509
They like to help, you know, sometimes.

2468
02:29:23.616 --> 02:29:25.379
Yes, Robert, I know.

2469
02:29:26.519 --> 02:29:29.215
He was arrested January 1975
for molestation.

2470
02:29:29.322 --> 02:29:31.222
He sent me that when he got out.

2471
02:29:31.324 --> 02:29:34.054
"Dear Dave, if I can ever be
of any help to you, just let me know.

2472
02:29:34.160 --> 02:29:35.991
"I'm sorry I wasn't your man."

2473
02:29:36.095 --> 02:29:37.653
And it's typewritten.

2474
02:29:37.763 --> 02:29:40.129
Using a typewriter is not a crime.

2475
02:29:41.601 --> 02:29:43.364
And he knew Darlene.

2476
02:29:44.770 --> 02:29:46.761
It's in the Vallejo files.

2477
02:29:51.978 --> 02:29:55.311
Mulanax said that
he was your favorite suspect.

2478
02:29:55.414 --> 02:29:59.373
That you spent two years on him,
and that nobody ever came close.

2479
02:30:02.455 --> 02:30:04.423
All the evidence said no.

2480
02:30:05.725 --> 02:30:07.955
Sherwood disqualified his handwriting.

2481
02:30:08.060 --> 02:30:11.188
The same Sherwood
that drinks like Paul Avery now?

2482
02:30:12.098 --> 02:30:14.032
Yes, you have Sherwood Morrill
in writing saying,

2483
02:30:14.133 --> 02:30:15.157
"I'm sorry, this just won't work."

2484
02:30:15.267 --> 02:30:17.030
- But you also have Terry Pascoe...
- His protege.

2485
02:30:17.136 --> 02:30:18.160
Yeah, fine, it's his protege,

2486
02:30:18.270 --> 02:30:20.101
but he's a handwriting expert
nonetheless, and he's saying,

2487
02:30:20.206 --> 02:30:22.907
"Do not disqualify this suspect
on the basis of handwriting."

2488
02:30:23.009 --> 02:30:24.943
- So the two cancel each other out.
- No, they don't.

2489
02:30:25.044 --> 02:30:26.341
It was Sherwood's case.

2490
02:30:26.445 --> 02:30:27.912
He was the head
of Questioned Documents.

2491
02:30:28.014 --> 02:30:29.345
If it went to trial,

2492
02:30:29.448 --> 02:30:32.417
all the defense would have to do
is call Sherwood to the stand.

2493
02:30:32.518 --> 02:30:35.146
And there was no way of getting Allen
into court in the first place,

2494
02:30:35.254 --> 02:30:36.482
because there was no evidence, Robert.

2495
02:30:36.589 --> 02:30:37.749
What do you mean,
there's no evidence?

2496
02:30:37.857 --> 02:30:38.949
You have him seen with the ciphers.

2497
02:30:39.058 --> 02:30:41.288
The military boot prints.
The same size shoes and gloves.

2498
02:30:41.394 --> 02:30:43.589
The Most Dangerous Game.
The Zodiac watch.

2499
02:30:43.696 --> 02:30:44.890
The background with school children.

2500
02:30:44.997 --> 02:30:46.828
The misspellings of Christ-mass.
The bloody knives.

2501
02:30:46.932 --> 02:30:48.797
All circumstantial.

2502
02:30:48.901 --> 02:30:51.631
Paul Stine's shirt, his wallet, his keys.

2503
02:30:51.737 --> 02:30:53.500
We should have found
one of those things in that trailer.

2504
02:30:53.606 --> 02:30:55.301
- We didn't.
- That's...

2505
02:30:57.743 --> 02:30:59.734
Okay. Catherine Allen states that

2506
02:30:59.845 --> 02:31:01.972
"Leigh cleaned out his trailer
on Friday after work

2507
02:31:02.081 --> 02:31:05.744
"and moved it to Santa Rosa
on Saturday, August 7th, 1971."

2508
02:31:05.851 --> 02:31:07.842
You interviewed him
at the refinery on August 4th.

2509
02:31:07.953 --> 02:31:09.477
- Yeah.
- So, he's cleaning out his trailer,

2510
02:31:09.588 --> 02:31:13.422
he's moving into a different county
48 hours after you interviewed him?

2511
02:31:15.027 --> 02:31:18.019
Okay. Okay.
Look at the stuff side by side, Dave.

2512
02:31:18.130 --> 02:31:19.222
All right.

2513
02:31:19.331 --> 02:31:22.095
Okay, Arthur Leigh Allen
and the Zodiac, their timelines.

2514
02:31:22.201 --> 02:31:24.863
- When was the first murder in Vallejo?
- Christmas, 1968.

2515
02:31:24.970 --> 02:31:27.564
Eight months before that,
Allen is fired for molesting his students

2516
02:31:27.673 --> 02:31:29.766
and his family discovers
that he's a pedophile.

2517
02:31:29.875 --> 02:31:32.173
- Now, when do the letters begin?
- July, '69.

2518
02:31:32.278 --> 02:31:33.939
After the murder of Darlene Ferrin.

2519
02:31:34.046 --> 02:31:37.106
And they continue
until you go to see him at work.

2520
02:31:37.216 --> 02:31:40.447
Now, after that, do any of the letters
contain swatches of Paul Stine's shirt?

2521
02:31:40.553 --> 02:31:42.350
No. Because he dumped them,
because he got scared.

2522
02:31:42.455 --> 02:31:44.184
Because he knew
that you were on to him.

2523
02:31:44.290 --> 02:31:48.021
- So, when's the next letter from Zodiac?
- Not until January of 1974.

2524
02:31:48.127 --> 02:31:49.526
He is silent for three years.

2525
02:31:49.628 --> 02:31:51.425
Then, in '74, he feels comfortable again

2526
02:31:51.530 --> 02:31:53.395
because everybody's moved off
Allen as a suspect.

2527
02:31:53.499 --> 02:31:54.488
And what do we get?

2528
02:31:54.600 --> 02:31:58.593
Three new letters from Zodiac
in January, May, and July in '74.

2529
02:31:58.704 --> 02:32:01.798
- But then the letters stop.
- What happens to Allen?

2530
02:32:05.344 --> 02:32:06.811
He's arrested.

2531
02:32:07.747 --> 02:32:11.080
January, 1975,
they send him to Atascadero.

2532
02:32:11.183 --> 02:32:14.084
We don't get another letter from Zodiac
the entire time he's there.

2533
02:32:14.186 --> 02:32:16.814
- When is he released?
- August, '77.

2534
02:32:16.922 --> 02:32:20.653
Allen gets out. He types you an apology,
and then what?

2535
02:32:20.760 --> 02:32:23.923
We get our first new Zodiac letter
in four years.

2536
02:32:29.568 --> 02:32:32.935
Okay. Zodiac had to have known
Darlene Ferrin, right?

2537
02:32:33.038 --> 02:32:35.268
Yes, because of the phone calls
on the night of her murder.

2538
02:32:35.374 --> 02:32:38.172
Because of the Vallejo file,

2539
02:32:38.277 --> 02:32:40.268
we know that Darlene knew
a man named Leigh?

2540
02:32:40.379 --> 02:32:41.368
Yes.

2541
02:32:41.480 --> 02:32:43.243
So, all coincidence aside, Robert,

2542
02:32:43.349 --> 02:32:46.147
how can you be sure that Leigh Allen
is the Leigh from this file?

2543
02:32:46.252 --> 02:32:48.720
Now, Vallejo is a small town,
but it's not that small.

2544
02:32:48.821 --> 02:32:50.118
How do you put
the two of them together?

2545
02:32:50.222 --> 02:32:53.385
This is a case that's covered
both Northern and Southern California,

2546
02:32:53.492 --> 02:32:55.858
with victims and suspects
spread over hundreds of miles.

2547
02:32:55.961 --> 02:32:57.690
- Would you agree?
- Yes.

2548
02:32:58.964 --> 02:33:01.762
Darlene Ferrin worked
at the Vallejo House of Pancakes

2549
02:33:01.867 --> 02:33:04.358
on the corner of Tennessee and Caroll.

2550
02:33:07.206 --> 02:33:11.939
Arthur Leigh Allen lived in his
mother's basement on Fresno Street.

2551
02:33:13.679 --> 02:33:17.046
Door to door, that is less than 50 yards.

2552
02:33:20.486 --> 02:33:21.953
Is that true?

2553
02:33:22.988 --> 02:33:24.478
I've walked it.

2554
02:33:28.327 --> 02:33:29.760
Jesus Christ.

2555
02:33:36.468 --> 02:33:37.457
So?

2556
02:33:41.407 --> 02:33:42.965
The prints, the handwriting...

2557
02:33:43.075 --> 02:33:46.044
- I'm not asking you as a cop.
- But I am a cop.

2558
02:33:48.914 --> 02:33:50.939
I can't prove this.

2559
02:33:51.050 --> 02:33:53.985
Just because you can't prove it,
doesn't mean it's not true.

2560
02:33:54.086 --> 02:33:55.713
Easy, Dirty Harry.

2561
02:33:59.325 --> 02:34:00.849
Finish the book.

2562
02:34:09.802 --> 02:34:12.270
Thank you. Thank you for breakfast.

2563
02:35:20.539 --> 02:35:22.029
Can I help you?

2564
02:35:23.709 --> 02:35:24.698
No.

2565
02:36:46.091 --> 02:36:47.422
Mr. Mageau.

2566
02:36:48.127 --> 02:36:50.425
Thanks for coming to see me.

2567
02:36:50.529 --> 02:36:51.860
You're the one I talked to on the phone?

2568
02:36:51.964 --> 02:36:55.491
I'm George Bawart. Vallejo PD.
I took over for Jack Mulanax.

2569
02:36:56.535 --> 02:36:59.504
It's been 22 years.
I don't know how I can help you.

2570
02:36:59.605 --> 02:37:00.765
Well, this is just a formality.

2571
02:37:00.873 --> 02:37:02.272
I'm gonna show you
a group of photographs.

2572
02:37:02.374 --> 02:37:04.239
Now, the person that shot you
may or may not be

2573
02:37:04.343 --> 02:37:06.368
among these photographs.

2574
02:37:06.478 --> 02:37:07.672
You don't have to pick anybody out

2575
02:37:07.780 --> 02:37:09.941
just because I'm showing you
these pictures, you understand?

2576
02:37:10.049 --> 02:37:11.573
Yes, sir, I do.

2577
02:37:12.484 --> 02:37:13.815
All right.

2578
02:37:14.853 --> 02:37:16.343
Take your time.

2579
02:37:16.855 --> 02:37:19.653
If you don't recognize anyone,
that's okay.

2580
02:37:31.136 --> 02:37:32.467
That's him.

2581
02:37:33.972 --> 02:37:35.906
How sure are you?

2582
02:37:36.008 --> 02:37:37.839
Yeah, I'm pretty sure.

2583
02:37:40.546 --> 02:37:41.672
He had a round face like this guy.

2584
02:37:41.780 --> 02:37:42.974
Wait. Am I to understand

2585
02:37:43.082 --> 02:37:44.845
that you're now identifying
the second photograph?

2586
02:37:44.950 --> 02:37:48.010
No, no. Just that
he had a round face like that.

2587
02:37:50.089 --> 02:37:51.556
It's this man.

2588
02:37:52.491 --> 02:37:53.788
All right.

2589
02:37:55.627 --> 02:37:58.687
Now, on a scale of one to 10,
10 being positive,

2590
02:38:02.801 --> 02:38:04.393
how sure are you?

2591
02:38:08.173 --> 02:38:09.800
At least an eight.

2592
02:38:12.611 --> 02:38:16.445
The last time I saw this face
was July 4th, 1969.

2593
02:38:19.718 --> 02:38:22.414
I am very sure
that's the man who shot me.
